; The file routines, one a module (a segment of its own each). Their INT 21h
; calls were seen in a -dos trace of a start up to the map (open 78 times at
; S2C8E:0047, close at S2B85:0015, reads at S2B8F, S2C01 and S2C45, the
; allocation at S2CBE:0037); what the arguments mean is read from the code.
name S2C8E:0006 file_open
comment S2C8E:0006 file_open(mode, far name): INT 21h AH=3Dh, AX = handle or 0. Mode 1 takes another path (presumably create; not checked).
name S2B85:0002 file_close
comment S2B85:0002 file_close(handle): INT 21h AH=3Eh.
name S2B8F:000C file_size
comment S2B8F:000C file_size(far name): opens, reads eight bytes to S2B8F:00C1; DX:AX = for a packed file (its signature) the unpacked length of the header, else the size from a seek to the end, FFFFh:FFFFh when it cannot be opened. The port's translation gives the original's lengths for the two files of the start.
name S2B81:0004 file_load_size
comment S2B81:0004 file_load_size(far place, far name, far work buffer): file_load, then DX:AX = file_size(name) whatever the load returned.
name CODE:04CB ptr_move
comment CODE:04CB ptr_move: the far pointer at DX:AX moved on by CX:BX bytes, its offset below 10h afterwards (the compiler's helper for a huge pointer).
name CODE:0553 ptr_add
comment CODE:0553 ptr_add: DX:AX = the far pointer DX:AX moved on by CX:BX bytes, its offset below 10h.
name S331F:4CBB map_number
comment S331F:4CBB map_number: the number of the battle's map, as game_loop puts it into the names of the map's files (set to 0 at the start; the menu sets it, not read).
name S2C01:0006 lib_read
comment S2C01:0006 lib_read(far place, far file, far names, far pointers, far work): for each name of the list (8 bytes each, ended by an empty one) the library's 12-byte table (its offset the file's first dword) is searched from its start (mem_same, eight bytes); the entry's data, up to the next entry's offset or the table, is read to place, unpacked by tpwm_unpack through work when it begins with "TPWM" and work's segment is not 0; its far pointer goes to pointers, place moves on (ptr_norm). Ends with 0:0 behind the pointers and returns place; FFFF:FFFF when the file cannot be opened or an entry is missing. Its reads go through S2C01:0230 (12 bytes). Read whole; translated (port/src/pictures.c).
name S2C45:0002 file_load
comment S2C45:0002 file_load(far place or 0/FFFFFFFF, far name, far work buffer of 1000h bytes or 0): each try writes 0 to DATA:0B17, then opens (up to four tries with a message when DATA:0376 is set), reads eight bytes to S2C45:0486; with a work buffer and the packer's signature there the file is unpacked, else read whole; allocates when no place is given. Returns the place, its offset made 1 to 10h, or 0.
; The packed file: the signature, the unpacked length as a dword, then
; groups of a control byte and eight items, bit 7 first: bit clear, one byte
; as it is; bit set, two bytes: the upper four bits of the first and the
; second are how far back (12 bits), the lower four plus 3 how many bytes
; to repeat from there. One byte more than the length is written, and the
; word behind the data is kept and put back. The file is read through the
; work buffer 1000h bytes at a time. Compared with the port's translation
; on the 47 calls of a start up to the first map.
name S2C9E:0002 ptr_norm
; file_name(where, folder, far name or 0, ending): puts a file's name
; together at name_buf and returns that: with where 2 the text at
; name_prefix first, then entry `folder` of name_dirs (6 bytes each), the
; name, and entry `ending` of name_exts (5 bytes each); a folder or ending
; below 0 is left out. Compared with the port's translation.
name S1571:02CD file_name
name S3310:00B9 name_buf
name S3310:007D name_prefix
name S3310:0029 name_dirs
name S3310:0041 name_exts
; num_text(long value, far to, width, flags): the value's amount in decimal
; at `to`, at most 10 places (the lowest digits when there are more); flags
; 4 fills up from the left, with spaces when 1 is set too, else with
; zeros. Compared with the port's translation.
name S2892:0001 num_text
comment S2C9E:0002 ptr_norm(far pointer): DX:AX = the same place with an offset below 10h.
name S2CBE:000E mem_alloc
comment S2CBE:000E mem_alloc(dword size): INT 21h AH=48h for size/16+1 paragraphs; the segment is entered in the table at DATA:0469 (count at DATA:0467) and returned in DX, AX = 0.

; Shows a text of GAME.TXT by its number in one side's status line: its
; callers pass 3Eh, 52h and 64h where the screen shows the quit question,
; the F1 line and the thinking time (runs with screenshots).
; With -1 it only fills the side's status line (x 5 to 94h, the second
; side's A0h further, y BCh to C4h) with colour D7h through the record
; DATA:0092 points to (DATA:00DA: colour, x0, y0, x1, y1) and S28E5:0004,
; and returns at S10AF:009B. Another text is then drawn from the table of
; word offsets the far pointer S331F:17BA points to, by S2B45:0006 at
; x 3Eh (plus A0h) less 3/2 of its length (CODE:2BD8 counts it), y BDh, colours
; 73h (75h for the second side), and game_state's word 0 gets 4 (8);
; RETF at S10AF:0130. Translated whole (port/src/draw.c) and compared.
name S10AF:000F show_message
comment S10AF:000F show_message(text number, side)
comment S28E5:0004 rect_fill: lines y DATA:00DE to 00E2 by S28FA:0000, DATA:00DE counted past the last. Translated (port/src/draw.c).
comment S28FA:0000 line_fill: one line from x DATA:00DC to 00E0 at y DATA:00DE in colour DATA:00DA on the page drawn, Mode X masks from its own segment (00A6, 00AA, words at 009E). Translated (port/src/draw.c).
comment S2B45:0006 text_draw(x, y, gap, line, colour, far text, far font, far map): each character's picture (font + map's word for it; FFFFh a gap of half the last width; 0:0 font and map take DATA:036A and 036E) by S2A6B:0008, then x on by its width (word 0Eh) and gap; '|' or 0Dh a new line. Translated (port/src/draw.c).
comment S2A6B:0008 pic_draw(x, y, far pic, dword colours, base): by byte 9 of the picture: 'P' to S2A76:0002 (y negative: S2A95:000E with -y), 'X' to S2957:0002, else S2AAF:0000. Translated (port/src/draw.c, pic_draw) but for the 'X' way.
comment S2A95:000E pic_half: a 'P' picture at -y drawn at half its size, uncut: four passes from the plane of x on, of plane 0's then plane 2's source rows (every second row), high halves in the first two passes, low in the last two. Translated (port/src/draw.c), compared through fight_panel.
comment S2A6F:0002 pic_unpack_draw(x, y, far pic, dword colours, base, far work): tpwm_unpack of pic to work, then pic_draw of work (of pic when DX is FFFFh: not packed). Translated (port/src/draw.c).
comment S2A76:0002 pic_blit_4: 4-bit pixels plane by plane, two a byte, base added, byte 8 transparent; cut by S2A76:0139 to DATA:00EC-00F2 when DATA:00E8 is not 0. Translated (port/src/draw.c, the S2AE4:000C table call left out).
comment S2532:1A8F flag_lying(x, y, c1, c2, c3): three stripes 12 by 2 pixels by rect_fill. Translated (port/src/draw.c, flag_draw).
comment S2532:1BC3 flag_standing(x, y, c1, c2, c3): three stripes 4 by 6 pixels by rect_fill. Translated (port/src/draw.c, flag_draw).
comment S1571:0134 num_draw(value, x, y): the number's decimal digits on the stack, drawn by S2B45:0006 in the colour of word 0 of DATA:0092's record. Translated (port/src/draw.c).
comment S2AAF:0000 pic_blit_8: 8-bit pixels plane by plane, each plane's row width from S2949:0002, byte 8 transparent, base added; S2AAF:0107 cuts when DATA:00E8 is not 0. The uncut way translated (port/src/draw.c, pic_blit_u).
comment S2949:0002 plane_widths: CX = width: (width & 3) words of width/4+1, then the rest of four words width/4, at ES:DI.
comment S2955:0002 screen_at with plane: DI = row table DATA:00F8 + x/4, CH = 11h rotated left by x & 3.

