; Fills a list of 24 entries (far pointer, dword length) with what a saved
; game holds after its header; save_game writes them in order (read from the
; code; their lengths add up to the size of a file a run wrote; the list is
; in tools/savfiles.py and docs/HANDOFF.md). Presumably load_game uses it
; too (it is called from two places; not read).
name S1273:0662 save_blocks

; Where three data files lie in memory: a -ram dump after 300 s of play holds
; the unpacked WW1GNDS.DAT (1,050 bytes) and AMOK.DAT (36 bytes) unchanged at
; these addresses, and 3,385 of the 3,519 bytes of the unpacked top-level
; UNIT.DAT (33h records of 45h bytes; the game changes some while it runs).
name S331F:05A3 ww1gnds_dat
name S331F:09BD unit_dat
name S331F:4C7A amok_dat

; The units (docs/HANDOFF.md, the saved game's records): F1h records of 1Ah
; bytes at S331F:189C, addressed as record number times 1Ah plus a field's
; address. Names of fields are from one saved file and from the code that
; reads them; what is not said here is not known.
;   unit_count  byte 2: S02E6:2556 subtracts a value from it and, when it is
;               not above that value, sets 4 in byte 14h and takes the
;               unit out of its carrier's list. Presumably how many are left.
;   unit_flags  word 4: 8000h marks an unused record (S15C5:0594 writes it,
;               the loops over the table test it); the low byte was 4 for
;               side one's units, 5 for side two's, 6 for two others; bits
;               40h and 80h presumably tie two records together (S15C5:0594
;               frees the next or the one before with them; not checked).
;   unit_kind   byte 8: the map file's value halved.
;   unit_pos    word 0Bh: offset in the map block of the byte that holds the
;               unit's number.
name S331F:189E unit_count
name S331F:18A0 unit_flags
name S331F:18A4 unit_kind
name S331F:18A7 unit_pos
; 46h records of 1Ch bytes: two rows of seven unit numbers (above F0h is
; none, S02E6:2556 walks them), four map offsets, five bytes, a unit number.
; The tables at S331F:3A0E, 38F6 and 38BE have the same record.
name S331F:3116 carriers
; Far pointers to the two map blocks; the map's length in bytes (width times
; height times two), its width and its height, as map_load sets them.
name S331F:17B6 map_ptr
name S331F:17B2 map2_ptr
name S331F:4C9E map_bytes
name S331F:4CA0 map_width
name S331F:4CA2 map_height
; A far pointer to the map moves are made on, presumably the map of the
; side whose half it is (map_ptr or map2_ptr); used by moving out (not
; checked beyond that).
name S331F:17AE map_cur
; A word order 4 sets to 1. At a round's end game_loop sets it first: 1
; when the side whose attacks are run (side 0 with 2 in attack_pick, else
; side 1) has attackers (byte 15h of its record in sides), else 0. With 0
; the screen goes grey around attacks_run (fade_grey, fade_back); with 1
; and fight pictures on it goes dark before (fade_out) and comes back
; after (fade_in) unless take_picture is set. So a site taken in a round
; without fights leaves it 1 and game_loop's fade_back out: order 4 has
; done it already.
name S331F:4CAA site_taken
; The count of the depots built: the next record of sites_100 a depot
; gets (orders 0Bh and 0Dh stop at 0Ah).
name S331F:4CAE depot_count
; A byte set to 1 before the picture of a site taken; game_loop clears it
; before attacks_run and leaves its fade_in out after it when it is set.
name S3303:0021 take_picture

; map_load (read, not stepped in a run): loads the map file with
; file_load, takes width and height from bytes 1 and 3 of its header and
; points map_ptr behind the four header bytes. Then it marks every record
; of the units, of sites_400, sites_100 and carriers unused (8000h;
; sites_40 is not marked) and walks the fields. The
; first byte indexes ww1gnds_dat (6-byte records); of that record's word 0,
; bits 2 and 1 give a side (2, 1 or 0) and 400h, 100h or 40h add a record to
; the table at S331F:3A0E, 38F6 or 38BE. A second byte below F4h is a unit:
; halved it is the kind (below 33h), its bit 0 the side; unit_add is called
; with the next number from unit_total, and for a kind with 40h and 80h in
; unit_dat's word 0Dh twice, the second a row down for side 1 (a row up
; for side 0) with the kind plus one. What the three tables are in the game is not known. The part
; behind file_load was compared with the port's translation on six maps
; (none of them with a two-part unit or a kind with 2 in word 0Dh).
name S0E56:0329 map_load
; (from, to): copies map_bytes bytes; map_load ends with it, map to map2.
name S0E56:1D9B map_copy
; shp_load(name, buffer, ...): called after map_load; loads the map's .SHP
; file with file_load and makes the units that stand in sites. The file: a
; byte for each of the 33h kinds (bit 0 sets or clears 2 in the kind's word
; 0Fh in unit_dat), a count, then records of 12 bytes: the units' flag bits
; (the side), the table (0 sites_40, 1 sites_400, 2 sites_100, else
; carriers), the record's number, a byte for the record's bytes 16h and
; 17h, one for its byte 18h, seven kinds (above F0h none). Each unit is
; made by unit_add on the record's first field, gets 4000h in unit_flags,
; is counted in its side's record and stands in both rows of the record.
; Compared with the port's translation on the first load of six runs.
name S0E56:0079 shp_load
name S331F:4CAC unit_total
; unit_add(number, kind, map offset, flag bits): fills the unit's record from
; the kind's record in unit_dat (byte 0 to 0, 3 to 2, 4 to 3, 3Dh to 9, word
; 11h to 6, word 0Dh to unit_flags with the flag bits set too); a kind with
; 1000h in word 0Dh gets a record of carriers, its number in byte 0Ah.
name S15C5:0005 unit_add
name S15C5:04AE carrier_add
name S15C5:0594 unit_free
; (record number, map offset, side): a record at S331F:3A0E, 38F6, 38BE
; (site_add_40 takes the map offset first, and the side is its record's
; number and, with 4, its flags; map_load calls it with side 2 as well,
; which is the place of the first record of sites_100). Byte 18h starts as 0Fh, 0Ah and 14h there, bytes 16h and 17h
; as 1Eh, 14h and 32h, and the flags (word 19h) get 8, 10h and 4; carrier_add
; gives 20h. The four map offsets: site_add_400 the field, the one two
; columns left and the two between them; site_add_100 the field, the one
; below and the two beside that; site_add_40 the field four times. Which
; of the two side fields is taken by the parity of the field's number
; ((field>>1)&1, as the port's site_add_400 and site_add_100 have it),
; not of its column; the two parities are the same on maps of even width
; only, and all 72 maps' files give an even width (read from their
; headers).
name S15C5:024A site_add_400
name S15C5:032C site_add_100
name S15C5:040D site_add_40
; The three tables those routines fill: 10, 10 and 2 records of 1Ch bytes
; (sites_40: one for each side).
name S331F:3A0E sites_400
name S331F:38F6 sites_100
name S331F:38BE sites_40
; (mask): the number of the first record of carriers whose flags have a bit
; of the mask, FFFFh for none; unit_add asks for 8000h, an unused one.
name S15C5:01F7 carrier_find
; unit_find(mask): the first of the units 0 to F0h with a bit of mask in
; unit_flags, FFh for none (8000h: a free record).
name S15C5:01A7 unit_find

; From a -ram dump after 300 s of play on a map of 32 by 24 (107 units):
; three units had 0200h in unit_flags and another offset in word 0Dh than in
; unit_pos; the map behind map_ptr had their number at unit_pos and FFh at
; the other offset, the map behind map2_ptr the reverse. So the second map
; is presumably the map as it will be when the orders given are carried out
; and word 0Dh where the unit is ordered to. Byte 9 counts the units of a
; kind and side as 1, 3, 5 and so on in both dumps looked at.
; (word 0Dh has no label: the code reaches it through a pointer to the record)
name S331F:18A5 unit_serial
; Byte 1 of a unit: in dumps after 2400 s of play, 1 to 4 in the units that
; had lost some of unit_count and in a few others. Presumably it rises with
; fights; not watched.
name S331F:189D unit_exp

; The routine that takes a fight's losses off. A run with -watch on one
; unit's unit_count (a long run played again to 2400 s) saw the byte set once
; by unit_add (S15C5:0074) and then lowered by one five times, each time by
; the last store of this routine (S2487:0AAD). Its end was read: the argument
; points to a record with far pointers to two units (at 0 and 4) and to their
; kinds' records in unit_dat (at 0Ah and 0Eh); two losses are bounded by the
; units' counts and subtracted. For a kind with 4 in its word 0Fh the result
; goes to the unit's byte 3 instead, and unit_count becomes 0 when that
; reaches 0.
; How the losses are worked out was read and then checked: 39 fights of six
; long runs, memory dumped at this address and at S2487:0AB1 (the end), the
; losses worked out from the first dump and compared with the second; all 39
; the same (docs/HANDOFF.md has the arithmetic). Not met in those fights: a
; kind with 4 in word 0Fh, a loss of 12 or more before the bounds.
name S2487:000A fight_losses

; The helpers fight_losses calls, read from their code: DX:AX times CX:BX,
; a signed division of two long values on the stack (towards zero; the
; entries after it are the unsigned one and the remainders), DX:AX shifted
; left by CL. The fight's results agree with them.
name CODE:03A1 long_mul
name CODE:03DC long_div
name CODE:048A long_shl
; Stores its argument at DATA:11F6 and 0 at DATA:11F8; the bytes after it
; (not decoded, not seen run) multiply that long value and return 15 bits of
; it. Presumably the seed and the random number routine. fight_losses calls
; this through the fight record's pointer at 6Ah and draws no number itself.
name CODE:07AB rand_seed
name DATA:11F6 rand_state
; Called by fight_losses with row and column of both fields when the
; attacker's reach is above 1; in the 39 fights its result was the distance
; in fields that the losses agree with.
name S0E56:241F field_distance

; The record a fight is worked out from (S02E6:000F fills it, S3AEC:0008
; points to it): far pointers to the units at 0 and 4, their numbers at 8
; and 9, far pointers to their kinds at 0Ah and 0Eh and to their fields'
; records in ww1gnds_dat at 12h and 16h, the fields' map offsets at 1Ah and
; 1Ch, column and row of both at 26h to 2Ch, word 2Eh set when the target is
; one of the attacker's six neighbouring fields, per cent at 30h and 31h.
name S331F:181C fight_rec
; Carries out one side's attacks (read; its fights were seen through
; fight_losses, the rest not stepped). It walks the side's list of attacking
; units (far pointer at 11h of the side's record, their number in byte 15h),
; takes the target field from the unit's word 11h, fills fight_rec, shows the
; fight (fight_show) unless S37FF:0115 is set, raises the units' unit_exp and
; in the end calls unit_free for every unit with 4 in unit_marks.
name S02E6:000F attacks_run
; Called by attacks_run when fight pictures are on; calls fight_losses (the
; return address a breakpoint there showed) and then S2532:0008 with the
; counts before and after. Presumably that one draws the fight; not read.
name S2474:0005 fight_show
; Called by attacks_run for a unit whose count is 0 after a fight: notes the
; field in one of the 7-byte records at S331F:4C5E, writes the given byte
; (FFh there) as the field's unit and sets 4 in the unit's unit_marks; the
; same for the other half of a two-part unit. Read, not stepped.
name S02E6:208E unit_destroy
; carrier_losses(side, unit, loss), called by attacks_run after a fight
; for a fighter with 1000h in unit_flags: each unit in the side's row of
; seven of the carrier's record (byte 0Ah) loses `loss` of unit_count; one
; with no more than that gets 4 in unit_marks and its place FFh. Read,
; translated (port/src/orders.c); compared in the fights of m8_site only
; where no carrier fought (not checked otherwise).
name S02E6:2556 carrier_losses
; pictures_load(far place, far work, far palette buffer): loads what a
; battle's screen needs to the free end `place` and returns it moved on;
; called by game_loop's setup and again by attacks_run after a fight
; picture or a site taken. In order: lbm_show of the file of pict_name
; (GAME.IFF, drawn to the screen; loaded at the place, which does not move
; on, so the next file lies over it); the palette file named by
; num_text(S37FF:0112) with ending 4 (00.PAL) to the palette buffer, its
; 300h bytes copied to where palette_ptr points (far_copy); lib_load of
; the records lib_rnd (0159), 01E5 (exp) and 01A9 (bum); the file of
; bigunit_name with ending 5 (file_load_size) at bigunit_dat; two blocks
; of 1194h bytes, bigunit_buf and bigunit_ptrs; lib_read of the names at
; bigunit_list from that name with ending 3 (LIB), its far pointers to
; bigunit_ptrs, the work buffer 10h bytes into that block, the pictures
; at bigunit_pics (F3Ch bytes kept for them); lib_load of 01F9
; (newshop); umap_name made ...DATA with ending 5 to umap_dat; then its
; letters 6 and 0Fh W or S by pics_winter and the file of umap2_name when
; word S331F:0008 is 1, else of umap_name, with ending 3 to umap_lib; the
; file music_name to music_data, its digit by the ratio of the sides'
; unit counts (S02E6:3118 to 318B: '1' above 140h/100h, '3' below
; C0h/100h, else '2'; byte 2 of each side's record plus 1, swapped when
; the sides' bit 2 differs and the first has it), 213Ah bytes kept for
; it; sfx_load of sfx_name. A file that cannot be loaded goes to the
; error exit (S0CB6:1842 with 2), but lib_load of rnd and of bum return
; FFFF:FFFF instead. Read whole; translated (port/src/pictures.c) and
; compared on its first call on map 0 and map 8 (port/README.md).
name S02E6:2B87 pictures_load
; lbm_show(far place, far name, far work): loads an IFF picture to place
; (rounded up to even) and draws it at screen_seg:0, a line every
; screen_pitch bytes, unchained (map mask 3C4h index 2, four pixels a
; byte), the planes 11h, 22h, 44h, 88h in turn. Looks for "PBM " (else
; "ILBM", which clears S2B06:03DC), "BMHD" and "CMAP" behind it and
; "BODY" from the segment's offset 0, a word at a time (REPNE SCASW,
; 1388h words). Width, height, compression (byte 0Ah of BMHD's data) and
; planes (8) are kept at S2B06:03EA to 03F0; the CMAP's bytes go to
; palette. Only with compression 1: a PBM's lines are ByteRun1 pixels; an
; ILBM's lines one plane after another, each bit ORed into video memory
; as the plane bit S2B06:03F2 (read back through the read map); a
; picture wider than 168h and higher than F0h is unpacked to
; screen_seg:0 as bytes, (width+7)/8 a line. A run that goes past a
; line's end is cut there. Returns FFFF:FFFF, 0:0 when the file cannot be
; loaded; BX and CX the width and height. Read whole; the PBM path
; compared through pictures_load, the other two not met.
name S2B06:0000 lbm_show
; tpwm_unpack(far from, far to): unpacks the packer's data ("TPWM", its
; length, then the codes file_load unpacks too) from memory; returns the
; length, FFFF:FFFF without the signature. Below 64K and inside the
; segment the word behind the data is kept (S2CA0:01C9 to 01CE); else
; the count at 01C1 runs down to FFFF:FFFF and one byte more is written.
name S2CA0:0008 tpwm_unpack
; mem_same(far a, far b, n): 0 when the n bytes are equal, else FFFFh.
name S2CF7:0006 mem_same
; sfx_load(far place, far name, far work): file_load, the place it
; returns kept at sfx_data and the file's length (file_size) at sfx_size
; and returned; FFFF:FFFF when the file cannot be loaded. Read,
; translated as far as memory goes (port/src/pictures.c).
name S2F39:00FD sfx_load
name S30EF:0242 sfx_data
name S30EF:0246 sfx_size
; Names and places of pictures_load (seen at its return on map 0 and 8):
name S331F:024C pict_name
name S331F:022D bigunit_name
name S331F:0235 bigunit_list
name S331F:026C umap_name
name S331F:0275 umap2_name
name S331F:027E music_name
name S331F:028A sfx_name
name S331F:02D7 bigunit_buf
name S331F:02DB bigunit_pics
name S331F:02DF bigunit_ptrs
name S331F:02E3 bigunit_dat
name S331F:17A2 umap_dat
name S331F:179E umap_lib
name S331F:179A music_data
; num_text's buffer of pictures_load and S02E6:323E (presumably used by
; others too; not looked for).
name S331F:177C num_buf
; FFh after the menu by bit 2 of byte 8 of the map's CODES.DAT record,
; else 0: the pictures' and grounds' names get W, else S (presumably
; winter and summer; a guess).
name S37FF:012F pics_winter
; The screen: the segment lbm_show draws to (A000h in the runs), the bytes
; a line, the palette (300h bytes) and a far pointer to it.
name DATA:0354 screen_seg
name DATA:02F0 screen_pitch
name DATA:04E3 palette
name DATA:00CE palette_ptr
; lib_load(far name, far place, far work, far record, byte order): loads
; a library of pictures (file_load_size) to place. Its first dword is the
; offset of a table of 12-byte entries (eight bytes of name, the dword
; offset of a picture in the file), ended by one with offset 0; with
; order set lib_order sorts them first. Clears 12 bytes behind the file,
; makes the table a list of far pointers in place (normalised, the last
; one the file's beginning), and fills the record (14h bytes: the name at
; 0, the file's length at 0Ah, the list at 0Eh, the count of pictures at
; 12h). Returns the length less 4 a picture, FFFFh:FFFFh for a file that
; cannot be loaded (the early RETF at S0C66:006A). Its callers move the
; free end on by the record's length, not by what it returns. Read;
; translated (port/src/files.c) and compared on its 13 calls of a start
; on map 0 and on map 8 (port/README.md).
name S0C66:0009 lib_load
; lib_order(far place, far table, far record, far work): loads the
; record's list of names (ending 5, eight bytes each) to place and copies
; the table's entries behind it in the list's order, each looked for
; among the first as many entries as the list has names (str_ncmp); the
; result goes back over the table. A name not found is written on the
; screen (S2A08:000A) before S0CB6:0DA9 (not read; not met). Read,
; translated, compared through lib_load.
name S0C66:024E lib_order
; lib_pick(far list, count, far table, words, far to, far buf): for each
; picture n of the list whose number is the low byte of one of the table's
; words, ground_store puts it into video memory and its place goes to
; entry n of buf (the other entries are not written); then count entries
; of buf are copied to `to` (far_copy). Returns how many were stored.
; grounds_load calls it with the record at S331F:0145. Read, translated
; (port/src/pictures.c), compared through grounds_load.
name S0C66:0414 lib_pick
; ground_store(far picture): four planes of 90h bytes from byte 12h of the
; picture copied into video memory at the far pointer DATA:035C (pages_set
; sets AC58:0000), which moves on by 90h; returns where they went. Read,
; translated (port/src/pictures.c).
name S28F5:0006 ground_store
; grounds_load(far place, far work): the map's grounds into video memory:
; lib_load of partS/partW (S331F:0145, sorted; the letter at S331F:0149 by
; pics_winter) to place, behind it the map's file (num_text of map_number,
; ending 0) and the file named at S331F:0264 (ending 0), then lib_pick of
; the library's list by the words of both files with buf the work buffer
; and `to` S331F:02E7, which then becomes the list at S331F:0153 (what
; ground_blit draws from). The word at 282h of the screen's record behind
; DATA:0092 gets offset 0. place does not move on. The error exit
; (S0CB6:1842 with 2) for a file that cannot be loaded. Called by
; game_loop's setup and after load_game. Read, translated
; (port/src/pictures.c), compared on maps 0 and 8 (port/README.md).
name S02E6:323E grounds_load
; far_copy(far from, far to, dword n): n bytes, one at a time, forwards.
name S0CB6:187F far_copy
; str_ncmp: the C library's strncmp (as far as the second's end).
name CODE:2BFE str_ncmp
; libs_start(free end, work): lib_load of the records at S331F:0131
; (LIB\pal, sorted) and S331F:0159 (LIB\rnd) one behind the other; the
; error exit (S0CB6:1842 with 2) when one cannot be loaded; returns the
; free end moved on by both lengths. Read, translated (port/src/battle.c).
name S02E6:3484 libs_start
; Records of lib_load, 14h bytes each (names seen in two runs): pal, the
; part pictures (partS or partW, S02E6:323E), rnd, bum, exp, the one at
; 01F9 (newshop, pictures_load). The menu's six libraries (MNU*.LIB) have
; their records at S37FF:0008, 001C, 0030, 0044, 0058 and 006C.
name S331F:0131 lib_pal
name S331F:0145 lib_parts
name S331F:0159 lib_rnd
name S331F:01A9 lib_bum
name S331F:01E5 lib_exp
name S331F:01F9 lib_newshop
; unit_panel(unit, side): the unit's line in the side's status line (x 5,
; the second side's A5h): show_message(-1, side), a flag at x+7Ah, y BCh
; (S2532:1BC3 standing stripes 3Eh, 1, 11h for a unit with bit 0 of word 4,
; else S2532:1A8F lying stripes 0, 1, 11h), the count at x+6 (byte 3 when
; the kind has 4 in its word at S331F:09CC, else byte 2) by S1571:0134, the
; experience (byte 1, at most 6) as picture n-1 of the table S331F:01F3
; points to (kind 'U') with word 18h of DATA:0092's record C8h meanwhile,
; and without 2 in word 4 the kind's name (S331F:09E9) at x+28h, y BDh in
; colours 73h (75h). RETF at S10E1:000E. Translated (port/src/draw.c).
name S10AF:0131 unit_panel
; fight_panel(fight record, pictures): draws the fight's panel; with
; pictures 0 it calls fight_losses itself (fight_show does when they are
; on). Sets fight_rec_ptr. What it draws: picture 0 of lib_newshop by
; S2A6F:0002 at x 0 (A0h when the first unit has bit 0 of word 4), the
; flags, two boxes in FFh, the two units' large pictures (S131D:0C50,
; places 0 and 3), the two grounds (ground_blit at S331F:02C5/02C6, from
; fight_rec 1Eh and 22h), six steps of figures at S331F:02B9 (kind *
; 6 + step of the unit pictures, colours 20h/30h; a kind with 40h in word
; 4 whole by S131D:1F0D), a page shown each step, and without pictures
; the lost ones again from step 5 down in B0h/C0h. Translated
; (port/src/draw.c) and compared on one call with pictures and one
; without (port/README.md). Its time (read from
; S131D:1AB5 to 1F0D and counted in runs): with pictures a fade_in first
; (S131D:1AC8; game_loop or the fight before left the screen dark), then the marks on the
; map in six steps, each drawn and followed by wait_frames(6), then
; wait_frames(0Ch); with pictures wait_input(96h) and fade_out, without
; them the six steps back with wait_frames(6) each and wait_input(46h).
name S131D:178D fight_panel
; big_unit(place, kind, right): a kind's large picture in a place of the
; fight's panel (table S331F:020D, 8 bytes: x, y, the name's x and y):
; its BIGUNIT.LIB entry (name in bigunit_dat by the kind's byte 09D7h,
; strncpy CODE:2C39 to the stack) read by lib_read to bigunit_buf, then
; bigunit_pics and the unit drawn (S2A6F:0002, colours 40h; at half size,
; y negated, in places other than 1, the unit lower by byte 09D6h, halved
; there), the kind's name in 71h. Translated (port/src/draw.c).
name S131D:0C50 big_unit
; panel_whole(far unit, x, y, base): a unit of a kind with 40h in word 4
; on the fight's panel, two of the unit pictures. Translated, not met.
name S131D:1F0D panel_whole
; panel_sound(n): a sound of a step of the fight's panel (S2F39:06E3,
; 096A; not read). Not translated.
name S131D:1FF0 panel_sound
; Set when the fights are not shown as pictures: then fight_panel works
; the losses out and attacks_run counts the blasts down on the map itself
; (presumably an option of the setup; 0 in the key-script runs).
name S37FF:0115 no_fight_pics
; Byte 14h of a unit: 4 is set by unit_destroy and by S02E6:2556, and
; attacks_run frees the units that have it. 1 was seen in units ordered to
; move; what else the byte holds is not known.
name S331F:18B0 unit_marks
; Word 11h of a unit: attacks_run takes the field to attack from it (the
; offset of the field's first byte in the map).
name S331F:18AD unit_aim


; Fills the six words at S331F:17FB with the map offsets of the fields
; around the field whose offset it is given (FFFFh for one beyond the map's
; edge): above, upper right, lower right, below, lower left, upper left. A
; field in an odd column lies half a field lower than its neighbours in the
; even ones. Read; the per cent bytes of 39 fights agree with it.
name S0B15:0162 field_neighbours
name S331F:17FB neighbours
; Two units' unit_flags, 1 when the second is on the first's side: bit 0 of
; the first set, the second's bit 0; else bit 1 set, the second's bit 1;
; else the second's bit 0 clear. Read.
name S0CB6:0205 same_side
; fight_around(unit, other, map, side index): looks at the six fields around
; `other` (field_neighbours) and leaves 1 in `neighbours` for each that holds
; a unit which could attack `other` (its kind's word 6 has one of `other`'s
; unit_flags bits 3Ch, or bit 2 if `other`'s word 6 has it, and not 40h) and
; is on `unit`'s side (same_side), 0 for the rest; returns which of the six
; holds `unit`.
name S02E6:2834 fight_around
; Its argument less 6 until it is 5 or below: a direction around a field.
name S02E6:2802 dir_wrap
; fight_percent(attacker, target, map, side index), called by attacks_run:
; sets the two per cent bytes of fight_rec (30h, 31h). Both are 0 when the
; attacker is on none of the six fields around the target. Else 30h is the
; sum, over the other five fields around the target that fight_around marks
; for the attacker's side, of the byte of the table at S331F:0009 for how
; many places round from the attacker the field is (1 to 5); 31h is 50h for
; each of the attacker's two neighbouring fields next to the target that
; fight_around marks for the target's side, at most 96h. Read, then worked
; out from the 39 dumps made at fight_losses and compared with the record's
; bytes: all the same (0 to 150 and 0 or 80 occurred; 31h with both fields
; held did not). The test for 12Ch after the sum can never hold, the sum is
; a byte.
name S02E6:2635 fight_percent
name S331F:0009 around_percent

; The unit records (F1h of 1Ah bytes); unit_exp, unit_count and the other
; unit_ names are fields of the first.
name S331F:189C units
; The far pointer fight_losses takes its record through (fight_rec in the 39
; fights).
name S3AEC:0008 fight_rec_ptr
; Pairs of signed bytes, indexed by byte 5 of a field's record in
; ww1gnds_dat: what the ground adds to an attack and to a defence
; (fight_losses; the 39 fights agree).
name S3AED:0000 ground_bonus

; Byte 16h of the first 31h-byte side record (S331F:4D92). attacks_run
; takes from it whose attacks it carries out: with 2 here side index 0 and
; the map behind map_ptr, else index 1 and the map behind map2_ptr (read).
; In the 39 fights it was 1, and DI at fight_losses 1. What else the byte
; means is not known.
name S331F:4DA8 attack_pick

; site_free(record, row): for a 1Ch-byte record (a carrier's, called by
; unit_free; presumably also those of the three tables filled from the
; ground): calls unit_free for the seven units of the given row (0 or 1)
; and empties their places, lowers the counts that belong to the record's
; word 19h (with 10h byte 4 of the side's record and the second of
; site_totals, with 8 byte 3 and the first, with 20h the third) and writes
; 8000h to word 19h. The side is the row, unless bit 0 of word 19h says 1
; (with bit 1 set and bit 0 clear it stays the row, so a site of no side
; lowers that row's counts). Read; the port's translation agrees with the
; original in the runs port/README.md names.
name S15C5:06EA site_free
; How deep unit_free is in itself (through site_free); above 5 it returns
; at once, and it leaves the count raised when it returns early.
name S331F:17F2 free_depth
; Records of 7 bytes that unit_destroy fills (the slot is its argument): a
; field's map offset, a count-down started from blast_time, the field's
; first byte and the unit byte written to it, both as words. Presumably
; the explosions to be shown.
name S331F:4C5E blasts
name S331F:4C82 blast_time
; The two sides' records of 17h bytes: byte 2 the side's units, bytes 3 and
; 4 its records of two of the tables filled from the ground, a far pointer
; at 11h to its list of attacking units and their number in byte 15h.
name S331F:4D33 sides
; Three bytes after unit_total that site_free lowers.
name S331F:4CAD site_totals

; game_loop from S066A:0938 to S066A:0EE6, where it goes into its loop:
; the rest of a battle's setup (read 2026-10-04; the port's battle_begin
; is the part of it that draws nothing, compared with the original on six
; maps). The routines named here are called there.
; The 8Fh bytes of state the saved game holds. Word 0, bits as read: 1 set
; by game_loop before the menu, 2 at the end of the setup, 40h and 80h in
; the setup, 200h a saved game is to be loaded, 400h the map is one for a
; single player (the menu sets it from byte 6 of the map's record in
; CODES.DAT and then makes one side the computer's: the second below map
; 18h, else the first). The menu's exit (S167A:25C1) also sets S37FF:012F
; from bit 2 of byte 8 of that record (FFh when set, else 0); the grounds
; file and the pictures' names follow it (W or S). The rule holds on 13
; maps' dumps (among them 8 and 49, both FFh); the other 59 are predicted
; from CODES.DAT alone. Word 2: 1 one side is the computer's, 2 none, 4
; both, 8 an item of the menu (which, was not looked at).
name S331F:4CA4 game_state
; A record of 31h bytes for each side, presumably its half of the screen:
; word 0 the map offset of the field its cursor is on, word 2 that of the
; view's first field, words 0Ch and 0Eh the cursor's column and row in the
; view, 10h and 12h where that is on the screen. Byte 16h is attack_pick.
name S331F:4D92 views
; view_reset(record): clears a view's record (byte 1Bh 5, bytes 28h to 2Ah
; 1, 2, 1). Read.
name S0CB6:0CDA view_reset
; view_to_field(side, map offset): puts the side's view so that the field
; is shown, four columns and rows from the view's corner where the map
; allows (the view is 10 columns by 8 rows: the corner is at most the
; width less 10 and the height less 8, and even), and the cursor on the
; field. Read.
name S0E56:177C view_to_field
; view_cursor(record, side): from the cursor's column and row in the view
; its place on the screen (col_x, row_y or row_y_odd for an odd column; A0h
; further right for the second side) and its map offset. Read.
name S0CB6:0154 view_cursor
; Fills the three tables below: a row is 18h high, an odd column's fields
; lie 0Ch lower, a column is 10h wide.
name S0E56:000B view_tables
name S331F:3B36 row_y
name S331F:3B26 row_y_odd
name S331F:3B46 col_x
; field_bits_clear(mask): clears the mask's bits in all 1104h bytes of
; field_bits (FFh: the whole byte). What the bits are is not known
; (attacks_run writes 80h or 40h by the side).
name S0B15:000B field_bits_clear
name S331F:3B5A field_bits
; The sum of byte 2 of the kind (the defence of the fight) over all units
; in use, but for the first half of a unit of two parts and units with 4
; in their word 6; 64h more with 8 in game_state's word 2; times 4, 3 or 2
; for 4, 8 or 10h in byte 16h of the first side's record (FFh from the
; menu when nothing is chosen); at most 7EF4h. The setup keeps it at
; game_state+8Bh. Presumably what a score is measured against (not
; checked).
name S02E6:29D4 defence_sum
; computer_reset(side): empties what the computer's player keeps for a
; side in S39B6 (its 0Ch-, 20h- and 49h-byte records and the two tables of
; 9 bytes a unit). Called in the setup for a side with 2 in word 0 of its
; record.
name S1C74:01B4 computer_reset
; income_add(side): side_points[side] += side_income(side). Called once
; from game_loop's state 5 after attacks_run (S066A:3F2A, read). Verified
; in the generated source (the side in SI, the call, the add); no run
; reached a round's end, so 0 hits there.
name S131D:1745 income_add
; side_income(side): the sum of byte 16h+side of the side's records in
; sites_100 and sites_400 (word 19h low bits the side) plus that byte of
; the side's sites_40 record. Read; the owner meaning of the word bits is
; a guess, and an unused record (8000h, whose low bits are 0) would count
; for side 0 unless its stock bytes are 0 (not checked).
name S131D:1685 side_income
; The step handlers behind the table at S1E4B:0381 (computer_step; the
; kind is byte 0 of a step, read from the code only, none stepped but
; step_move, see computer_step below). step_move and step_attack move a
; unit and order an attack by scripted input; step_end_round goes to the
; side's sites_40 field and waits for the round's end bit; step_unit_out
; and step_site_menu (names are guesses) pick from a 1Ch record through
; unit_holder; step_build walks the build_kinds list. cursor_scroll and
; cursor_step write cursor moves into computer_script.
name S1E4B:0484 step_move
name S1E4B:06DF step_attack
name S1E4B:08ED step_end_round
name S1E4B:0A26 step_unit_out
name S1E4B:0D88 step_site_menu
name S1E4B:0FB8 step_build
name S1E4B:1464 cursor_scroll
name S1E4B:15E8 cursor_step
; unit_holder(side, b1): the 1Ch record of the kinds 4 and 6 (read;
; returns S331F, verified at its RETFs) and rec_find_unit (not read
; past its start). move_targets_list(work buffer, unit, from, side,
; map): lists the marked fields move_target gives 0 for at a far
; pointer, counted in path_len; it does not call path_find.
; holder_ptr and step_target_field are the far pointer and the chosen
; field (mislabeled DATA in the source; used with DS=S3AE8, as is
; S3AEB:0006 to 000F in computer_plan: the rebuild is unaffected since
; only offsets encode).
name S1E4B:1734 unit_holder
name S1E4B:1827 rec_find_unit
name S0B15:13EC move_targets_list
name S3AE8:001D holder_ptr
name S3AE8:0021 step_target_field
; clock_seed(far value): keeps the value at DATA:0AF1, or for 0 one made of
; the BIOS's count of timer ticks: the start of the random numbers
; rand_next gives. Called with 0 by the battle's setup in game_loop and by
; S2532:0008, the fight's pictures (seen in a run: once a fight shown,
; see docs/HANDOFF.md "The pass with the computer's own turn"); rand_range, which computer_queue draws what to
; build with, was the only caller of rand_next seen in that run (S2532 has
; calls of its own from S2532:183B on, not reached there).
name S2C95:000E clock_seed

; game_loop's loop from S066A:1F39 to its end (read 2026-10-04, nothing
; stepped; docs/HANDOFF.md, "The loop of game_loop, second reading", has
; what the states of a view do). The routines and places named here are
; used there.
; timer_set(kind, passes, value): the first free of the 15 timers in
; game_state (byte 19h the kind, dword 28h the pass it is due at: the count
; of passes at dword 13h plus the passes, word 64h the value) gets the
; kind; for kinds 1 and 2 the timers of their own kind are freed first.
; Nothing when no slot is free. Read.
name S0CB6:0272 timer_set
; timer_fire(kind, timer): what a timer does when game_loop finds it due
; at the end of a pass: 1 and 2 take the first and second side's message
; off (show_message(-1, side)) and clear 4 and 8 in game_state, 3 and 4
; set 20h and 40h in game_state's word 4, 5 calls S0E56:145A with the word
; of the timer's number at S331F:4D08, 6 and 7 clear 200h and 400h in
; game_state's word 4. Read.
name S0CB6:035A timer_fire
; A word for each side: what building a unit (byte 3Fh of its kind) and
; repairing one (0Fh, or 32h with 4000h in the unit's word 6) is taken
; from; shown at most as 2710h. Where it comes from was not looked at.
name S331F:02B5 side_points
; The number of kinds a site offers to build and their list, filled by
; build_list.
name S331F:17BE build_count
; build_list(points, side): build_kinds and build_count anew, the kinds the
; side may build for points (port/src/side.c says which); called when a
; site is entered in the attack half and after a repair (game_loop
; S066A:3232). Presumably also from where else it was seen to run at a
; round's end (map 0 run s4, t=208); that caller was not looked for.
name S131D:14D4 build_list
name S331F:17BF build_kinds
; view_step(view, input record, input bits, far pointer, side): what
; game_loop calls for a side whose view is in state 0 (byte 17h); by byte
; 18h it waits for the button (0, 19h) or lets the side choose where a unit
; moves (16h, 3) or whom it attacks (13h). Returns 0 with the button
; pressed. Read; docs/HANDOFF.md has the steps.
name S0CB6:0750 view_step
; field_menu(view, side, input bits): state 1 of a view, the choice on the
; cursor's field: makes the bits of what may be chosen (word 1Ch), lets a
; direction with the button held pick the pointer (byte 1Bh) and, when the
; button is let go, begins a move or an attack or sets the view's state (3
; the map, 4 the field's unit, 5 the round's end, 6 into a site). Read.
name S0CB6:0EAA field_menu
; view_copy(far view, back): bytes 0 to 27h of a view to the copy at
; S331F:4D61, or back from it with back not 0 (moving out keeps the view
; there; presumably for going back to it, not followed).
name S0CB6:0445 view_copy
; side_input(far input record, far view): the input word of a human side
; (game_loop puts it in DI): 10h the button, 4 left or 8 right, 1 up or 2
; down from the record's bytes (left, right, up, down, button; cleared),
; directions only when the view's repeat counter (byte 2Ch, from the
; delays at 28h by the stage in 2Bh) has run out or they changed.
name S0CB6:05F1 side_input
; view_draw(field, side): draws the 9 by 7 fields of a view from field
; (grounds by S331F:0153, units by S331F:013F through S2931:000E); a
; foreign unit with 2 in word 6 is not drawn. Presumably draws only (no
; write to the game's state seen); the name is a guess. Read whole: the
; field is a byte offset in the map (two bytes a field), the second side
; draws from map2_ptr at x A0h; the unit's picture is byte 0Fh + side of
; its record plus 6 times byte 8, colours 30h with bit 0 of word 4, else
; 20h. Translated (port/src/draw.c), compared on four calls (port/README.md).
name S0E56:0D44 view_draw
comment S290A:0006 ground_blit(x, y, far src): a field's ground, 16 by 24, copied in write mode 1 from video memory at src, then the hexagon's edge pixels plane by plane. Translated (port/src/draw.c).
comment S2931:000E unit_blit(x, y, colour base, far src): a unit's 24 by 24 picture, 4 bits a pixel from src+12h, plane by plane; byte 8 of src the transparent value; keeps the plane mask and that byte at S2931:00F8/00F9. Translated (port/src/draw.c).
; marks_draw(field, side): the view's fields' marks in field_bits (55h
; for the first side, AAh for the second) drawn through S0E56:24ED.
; Presumably draws only; the name is a guess. Read whole: field_bits has
; 40h fields a row; S0E56:24ED folds the side's bits to an index (8 more
; with byte 1Bh of the view 0 or 4) into the table of lo, hi, add at
; S330B:0008 (add FFh: nothing) and calls S2A1C:0004. Translated
; (port/src/draw.c), compared on seven calls (port/README.md).
name S0E56:0F36 marks_draw
comment S2A1C:0004 mark_blit(x, y, lo, hi, add): for each plane the offsets listed in its segment from 008Eh (each plane's list ended by a negative word); a pixel between lo and hi gets add. Its last OUT goes to port hi:lo (DX), so the map mask stays at plane 3. Translated (port/src/draw.c).
; field_draw(side, field, ...): draws one field when it lies in the
; side's view and the view is in state 0, 1, 7 or 8. Presumably draws
; only; the name is a guess.
name S0E56:145A field_draw
; marks_erase(field, side, mask): the view's fields from field that have
; mask in field_bits drawn again (without the marks), then
; field_bits_clear(mask). move_aim calls it before marking the way. The
; name is a guess.
name S0E56:1217 marks_erase
; rows_sync(table, side, other side, records): attacks_run calls it at a
; round's end for carriers, sites_100, sites_400 and sites_40 with the side
; whose attacks it carried out and the other. For each record without 8000h
; and 2 in word 19h: a record of the other side (same_side) has that side's
; row of seven copied to the first side's row, a freed unit (8000h in
; unit_flags) becoming FFh in both; any other record has the first side's
; row copied to the other's. So each side has its own row, as it has its own
; map, and a round's end makes them the same. Read, not stepped.
name S02E6:23F0 rows_sync
; Sets 8000h in unit_flags of every unit whose unit_count is 0 (attacks_run,
; at a round's end). Read, not stepped.
name S02E6:2B28 units_drop_empty
; Word 11h of game_state: attacks_run adds 1 at every second round's end
; (when attack_pick has become 1 again); presumably the number of the round
; the players see. Not checked.
name S331F:4CB5 round_count
; buf_neighbours(column, row): as field_neighbours, but the six entries of
; neighbours are places in a work buffer of one byte a field and 64 fields a
; row (column plus row times 64), not map offsets; FFFFh for those beyond
; the edge. S0B15:025F clamps the column and row to the map first (as the
; port's buf_neighbours has it). Read.
name S0B15:005B buf_neighbours
; move_costs(buffer, unit, side, mask, map): what entering each field costs
; the unit, as a negative byte in a buffer of 1104h bytes; B0h is a field it
; cannot enter. From the ground's record in ww1gnds_dat: B0h unless its
; byte 2 has a bit of the kind's byte 5; else minus its byte 4 for a unit
; with 10h in unit_flags, minus its byte 3 for the others; 10h in the
; unit's word 6 overrides either and pays 2 everywhere it may enter.
; B0h where the ground's word 0 has a bit of the mask
; (FFFFh is no mask). Then the units on the map: B0h for one with 2 in
; unit_flags and for one of the other side, whose six neighbours (not B0h)
; get 9Ah (around a unit of the second side) or 9Bh; FEh for a unit of the
; own side with 1000h or 2000h; and B0h for every field with another unit
; when the kind's word 0Dh has 40h. Read, not stepped.
name S0B15:0A01 move_costs
; move_range(field, buffer, unit, range, side, mask, map): where the unit
; can move. Keeps its nine argument words at S3306:000A, calls move_costs,
; puts the range on the unit's field and spreads it: a neighbour gets what
; is left less its cost if that is not below 0, and 0 if it lies beside a
; unit of the other side (9Ah, 9Bh), so that the move ends there. Only the
; fields from half the range left of and above the unit's to the range
; further on are looked at. Every field that was reached gets 1 (first
; side) or 2 in field_bits; returns their number, the unit's own among
; them. Read, not stepped.
name S0B15:0371 move_range
; The nine argument words of the last move_range call; view_step's step
; 18h calls it again with them.
name S3306:000A move_args
; attack_range(buffer, field, range, side, unit, mask, map): whom the unit
; can attack. Marks the fields less than the range away (those around the
; unit's own are taken out with 40h in the mask) and of them keeps those
; with a unit of the other side (not one with 2 in unit_flags) whose
; unit_flags have one of the mask's bits 3Ch, or whose word 6 has 2 with 2
; in the mask. They get 4 (first side) or 8 in field_bits; returns their
; number as a byte. Read, not stepped.
name S0B15:062F attack_range
; unit_mark(unit, bits, side, set): sets or clears the bits (100h or 200h)
; in the unit's unit_flags and, on its field, 40h or 80h (for 100h; by the
; side) or 10h or 20h (for 200h) in field_bits, draws the field
; (S0E56:145A) and does the same for the other half of a two-part unit.
; Read as far as that; not stepped.
name S0E56:1DDB unit_mark
; attack_order(view, map, side): the button on a field while a unit (word
; 1Eh of the view) chooses whom to attack. On a field marked 4 or 8 for the
; side: an ordinary unit gets the field in unit_aim, 2 in unit_marks, 9 in
; its byte 13h and is put on the side's list of units with an order (text
; 49h); one with 4000h in word 6 gets 0Bh in byte 13h, or 0Dh on a ground
; that is the byte at S331F:4C92 (text 46h; 47h and nothing when the byte
; at S331F:4CAE has reached 0Ah); one with 2000h gets 11h (text 6Eh). Each
; is marked with 200h (unit_mark). Any other field: text 45h. Returns 1
; when an order was given. Read, not stepped.
name S0AE0:0008 attack_order
; attack_unmark(far view, side): what view_step does after attack_order
; (step 13h): field_bits_clear with 4 (8 for the second side), unit_mark of
; the view's unit (word 1Eh) taking 100h away, then view_draw and
; marks_draw. The name is a guess from what it changes.
name S0AE0:02E3 attack_unmark
; move_aim(view, map, side): the button on a field while a unit chooses
; where to move. Refuses (12h) a field not marked 1 or 2 for the side, the
; unit's own, a ground with 4000h in its word 0 for a unit with 10h in
; unit_flags, one S10E1:0F82 gives a text for, and one S0B15:0E52 finds no
; way to (text 48h). Else the way's fields (their number at S331F:17F3,
; the fields at 1F40h in the side's work buffer) are the only ones left
; marked, the field goes to unit_aim and the result is 1; 8 is added for a
; two-part unit. Read, not stepped; the two routines it calls not read.
name S10E1:02EB move_aim
; move_start(view, side): the button again on the field move_aim took: the
; unit is put on the side's list of units with an order, unit_aim becomes
; its own place, 80h is set in game_state's word 4 and a timer of kind 4
; started (which presumably moves it along the way). Returns 1, or 12h
; for another field. Read, not stepped.
name S10E1:05D1 move_start
; move_done(view, map, side, flags): ends the choosing of a move: clears
; the side's marks 1 or 2 and draws the view. With 10h in the flags the move
; is given up: 100h is cleared in unit_flags, 40h or 80h in field_bits, and
; a unit that was moving out of a site or carrier (byte 19h of the view 3)
; is taken off the map and put back in its place there, the view going back
; to state 2. Read, not stepped.
name S10E1:000F move_done
; path_find(buffer, unit, from, to, side, map): the way of a unit over the
; fields move_range marked for the side (1 or 2 in field_bits). Fields are
; kept in the buffer as records of 10 bytes (column, row, the record it was
; reached from, its worth, the records before and after it in the order of
; worth) and tried in that order; the worth of a field is its distance to
; the end times the kind's byte 15h plus the ground's cost (byte 3 of its
; record, byte 4 for a unit with 10h in unit_flags) times the kind's byte
; 16h. 40h or 80h in field_bits marks a field met and is cleared at the
; end. Returns 0 with the way, from its end back to its beginning, as map
; offsets at 1F40h of the buffer and their number in path_len; FFFFh
; without one or with more than 316h records. Read; compared with the
; port's translation.
name S0B15:0E52 path_find
name S331F:17F3 path_len

; How a move is carried out (read 2026-10-04; docs/HANDOFF.md, "The walk").
; move_rec: the one move under way. Byte 0 the unit, byte 1 the unit on the
; aim's field, byte 2 the unit byte of the map the unit stands on (put back
; when it goes on; FFh at the start, byte 1Bh of the site's record for a
; unit moving out of one), byte 3 the same under the second half of a
; two-part unit, byte 4 a place in a row of seven, far pointer 5 the site's
; or carrier's record and byte 9 its number, word 0Ah the aim's field, byte
; 0Ch what the arrival is (1 to 5, see move_arrive). Only one unit walks at
; a time: move_start sets 80h in game_state's word 4, which field_menu
; tests.
name S331F:180F move_rec
; move_step(): game_loop calls it at a pass's end with 40h in game_state's
; word 4 (what a timer of kind 4 sets when due). Takes the unit of move_rec
; one field on along the way path_find left (the word at path_len in the
; list at 1F40h of its side's work buffer; the side is bit 0 of
; unit_flags): its field on the side's map gets back what move_rec keeps,
; the next field's unit byte is kept and becomes the unit, the unit's byte
; 0Fh (10h for the second side) the direction (field_dir), its unit_pos for
; the side the field; the second half of a two-part unit (the next record)
; follows onto the field the first left. carrier_moved for a carrier. With
; fields left: a timer of kind 4 over the kind's byte 17h passes, path_len
; one less. On the last field move_target is called first, and afterwards
; move_arrive, whose text is shown; 8 or 10h set and 80h cleared in
; game_state's word 4, 100h cleared in unit_flags (both halves). Read;
; the fields are drawn by S0E56:145A (not read).
name S10E1:072C move_step
; move_target(field, side, map): what a move to the field would be, kept in
; move_rec (byte 0Ch, word 0Ah and what the kind needs); returns 0 or the
; number of the text that says why not.
; - A unit on the field (byte 1 of move_rec; the first half for a second
;   half): text 37h for one of the other side, 39h for one that is no
;   carrier (1000h), 3Ah when the mover's word 6 and the carrier's record's
;   word 19h share none of the bits 0FC0h or the carrier has 200h, 3Bh
;   without a free place in the side's row, when the load (row_load of the
;   carrier, the mover's kind's byte 41h and, for a mover that is a carrier,
;   its own row_load) is above the carrier's kind's byte 40h, or when a
;   carrier moving in has more units than the other has free places less
;   one. Else kind 2 with the first free place.
; - A ground with 400h, 100h or 40h in its word 0: the record of sites_400
;   or sites_100 with that field (site_find), or of sites_40 by bit 0 of
;   the ground's word. A site not of the side, or with 2 in its word 19h:
;   kind 4. An own one: kind 5 with the first free place, 3Bh without one
;   (or for a carrier with too many units, as above).
; - Else kind 3; text 40h when the ground's byte 2 has no bit of the kind's
;   byte 5, or for a unit with 10h in unit_flags on a ground with 4000h.
; Read. Also called by move_aim, by S0B15:13EC (which lists the marked
; fields it gives 0 for at a far pointer, counted in path_len) and at
; S1E4B:0621 (the computer's player).
name S10E1:0F82 move_target
; move_arrive(side, map): the end of a walk, by byte 0Ch of move_rec; the
; unit gets that kind in byte 13h (its order), 1 in unit_marks, and (in
; kinds 3 and 4) the details in bytes 15h (the record's number), 16h (the
; other unit), 19h (the place) and word 17h (the record's flags, or in
; kind 1 the other unit's unit_flags); kind 2 does not write word 17h,
; kind 5 not byte 16h, kind 1 not byte 15h (as the port's move_arrive has
; them). Returns the text (38h but in kind 1).
; - 3, a field: 200h for 100h and 4000h in unit_flags (unit_mark).
; - 4, a site of the other side or of nobody: the same; the site is not
;   changed here.
; - 2, into a carrier: the unit is put in the place of the side's row, the
;   carrier's number back on the field, 4200h for 100h in unit_flags; a
;   carrier's own units go over to the other (row_move).
; - 5, into a site of the side: the same with the row of the site, the
;   unit byte of the field becoming F4h and the unit's place the site's
;   word 0Eh.
; - 1: the unit on the field (byte 1) goes into the mover's own row and
;   gets 4200h, the mover takes the field (text 43h with 20h in the other
;   unit's word 6, else 44h). No routine read so far writes kind 1 to
;   move_rec; presumably not reached (not checked).
; Read.
name S10E1:0AF0 move_arrive
; field_dir(from, to): the direction of a neighbouring field as map
; offsets, 0 above and on clockwise to 5. Read.
name S10E1:144C field_dir
; order_undo(unit, map, side): takes back what move_arrive did, by the
; unit's byte 13h: 2 and 5 empty the unit's place in the carrier's or
; site's row (the table of a site by 4 and 8 in word 17h: sites_40,
; sites_400, else sites_100), 3 and 4 take the unit (and the other half)
; off the map, 1 puts the other unit back on the field with its flags and
; empties the place in the mover's row. Clears 1 in unit_marks, 4200h in
; unit_flags and byte 13h. attacks_run calls it for a unit that is to be
; freed (4 and 1 in unit_marks) and for the units in such a carrier. Read.
name S10E1:1514 order_undo
; row_count(side, record, used): how many of the seven places of the
; side's row hold a unit (used not 0) or are free. Read.
name S10E1:17D9 row_count
; row_move(side, record, to): each unit of the side's row of the first
; record goes to the first free place of the other's row, its unit_pos for
; the side becoming the other's word 0Eh. Read.
name S10E1:184E row_move
; row_load(record, side): the sum of byte 41h of the kinds of the units in
; the side's row. Read.
name S131D:15FB row_load
; carrier_moved(unit, side): gives the carrier's place (unit_pos for the
; side) to the units in the side's row of its record and to the record's
; word 0Eh. Read.
name S15C5:0804 carrier_moved
; site_find(field, table): the number of the first of the table's ten
; records with the field among its four map offsets (0Eh on), FFFFh for
; none. Read.
name S0E56:1726 site_find
; depot_places(field, map): field_menu's test for a unit with 4000h in
; word 6 (the builder of depots). The ten fields at depot_steps from the
; field (a map offset) go into `neighbours`; one is kept when its ground is
; amok_dat's byte 18h (presumably a depot's) or when its four fields of
; foot_steps all lie on the map with a ground with 8000h and no unit (byte
; 1 above F0h), else its entry becomes FFFFh. No test of the map's edge for
; the ten. Returns the number kept. Read; the port's translation agreed
; with the original through field_menu (port/README.md).
name S0E56:18A3 depot_places
; Ten signed column steps and ten row steps for a field in an even column
; (0021, 002B), then the same for an odd one (0035, 003F); depot_places
; reads them.
name S331F:0021 depot_steps
; footprint(field): the four fields of a depot on the field (a map offset)
; as map offsets into `neighbours`: column and row of the field plus the
; signed steps of foot_steps, the first of which is the field itself (the
; same four site_add_100 takes). No test of the map's edge. Called by
; attacks_run's orders 0Bh (S02E6:17C3) and 0Dh (S02E6:189E) only. Read;
; the port's translation agreed with the original on two passes.
name S0E56:1A97 footprint
; Four signed column steps and four row steps for a field in an even column
; (0049, 004D), then the same for an odd one (0051, 0055). Only footprint
; reads them, through far pointers it builds itself.
name S331F:0049 foot_steps
; aim_grounds_set(place, aim, map): order 11h of attacks_run (S02E6:1986,
; its only caller; a unit with 2000h in word 6). From the columns and rows
; of the two map offsets an index: the place's column parity times 36h, the
; aim's column less the place's plus 1 times 12h, the rows' the same times
; 6. It chooses three fields by aim_steps; each whose ground has 8000h in
; its word 0 gets its byte of aim_grounds, or, when the aim's ground is A5h
; or above at entry, 51h (presumably taking the work back; that branch was
; not seen run). No test of the map's edge. Read; one pass on map 51
; agreed with the port.
name S0E56:1B57 aim_grounds_set
; aim_steps: for each index of aim_grounds_set three pairs of signed column
; and row steps from the place. In the entries looked at (an even column;
; the aim above left, left below, above and below) the second pair is the
; aim itself and the two others are the aim's neighbours to either side of
; the line from the place: three fields in a row across that line. The
; entries for an aim that is no neighbour of the place are all 0 (the place
; itself, three times). The other entries were not looked at one by one.
name S331F:0059 aim_steps
; aim_grounds: with the same index the ground each of the three fields
; gets; only the first byte of each pair is read. The second field's (the
; aim's) differs from the two others', which is how the test for A5h at
; entry finds an aim worked on before (presumably; not checked that all
; three are A5h or above for every entry).
name S331F:00C5 aim_grounds
; ---- The computer's player (2026-10-07). It plays a side through the same
; hand a human has: what it wants to do becomes a list of steps, a step
; becomes a script of input codes, and each pass of game_loop takes one
; word of direction and button bits from that script in place of what
; S0CB6:05F1 reads for a human.
; computer_turn(side): one pass of a computer's side, called by game_loop
; in place of reading the side's input. Sets the side's text in
; computer_out to 4Eh and then serves the phase word of computer_phase:
; 20h computer_assess (text 61h), 40h computer_plan (text 62h or 63h, byte
; 0Bh of the record flips each pass), 8 computer_queue (text 60h); each
; phase's routine is called once a pass and the phase goes on (20h to 40h
; to 8 to 2, byte 46h of computer_steps set to 0) when it returns not 0.
; Then, in the same pass: 2 computer_step (text 4Fh), not 0 from it goes
; back to 8, 0 on to 1 with the script's place (byte 1Eh of
; computer_script) set to 0; and 1 computer_input (text 4Fh), not 0 from
; it back to 2. Read and stepped: runs of both sides logged every call and
; what each routine returned, in this order (the second side on map 0, the
; first on the maps of the codes 24 and 30).
name S1C74:000B computer_turn
; A record of 0Ch bytes for each side. Word 0 the phase (20h, 40h, 8, 2,
; 1 as computer_turn has them; game_loop sets 4 after a round's end, not
; read here what for), byte 3 the state of computer_queue (0 to 8), byte
; 0Bh which of the two texts computer_plan's phase shows. The other bytes
; were not read.
name S39B6:12FD computer_phase
; A record of 20h bytes for each side: the script of input codes, ended by
; FFh; byte 1Eh the place in it, byte 1Fh the place in a code's sequence.
; Its first byte is FFh while there is none.
name S39B6:1224 computer_script
; A record of 49h bytes for each side: up to ten steps of 7 bytes (byte 0
; the kind, 1 to 7, FFh ends the list; the rest what the kind needs), byte
; 46h the number of steps while they are queued and the step being carried
; out afterwards, byte 47h the state inside a step (0 to 7 for kind 1),
; byte 48h not read.
name S39B6:126B computer_steps
; Two words for each side: the direction and button bits game_loop takes
; as the side's input (1, 2, 4, 8 up, down, left, right, 10h the button),
; and the number of the text it shows for the side.
name S39B6:1315 computer_out
; computer_assess(side), computer_plan(side) and computer_queue(side): the
; routines of the phases 20h, 40h and 8; each does a part of its work a
; call and returns not 0 when done (seen: 6 calls of computer_assess, 321
; to 1650 of computer_plan, 6 to 82 of computer_queue a time).
; computer_queue goes by byte 3 of computer_phase through nine states
; (table at S1CC6:0A23) and adds the steps with step_add; its first state
; sets word 2 to FFFFh in the record of each unit of the side in the table
; of 9-byte records (S39B6:0132 or 09AB by attack_pick). All three are
; described below.
name S1CC6:0A35 computer_assess
name S2138:000C computer_plan
name S1CC6:0000 computer_queue
; ---- computer_assess, read in full (2026-10-07, Mac). It goes by byte 5
; of the side's computer_phase through five states, one a call, and
; returns 1 from the sixth (byte 5 back to 0):
; 0: byte 7 of computer_phase 0; with 2 in the side's attack_pick nothing
;    more (on to state 5). Else every unit without 8002h in unit_flags is
;    weighed by unit_worth, the three words summed up for the side's own
;    units and for the others; word 9 of computer_phase becomes 3 when
;    twice the own sum is not above the others', 2 when the own sum is
;    below it, else 1 (presumably how careful the side is to be). An own
;    unit's plan is emptied (word 0 0, word 4 FFFFh, byte 8 0, and the same
;    three in unit_plans2 whichever table is the side's), but not with 0Bh
;    in its byte 8, not with 9 there while unit_reaches finds a way to one
;    of the fields of sites_list (the side's sites, with 0Fh points or
;    more), and a unit with 1000h in unit_flags (a carrier) that holds a
;    unit with 4 in its word 6 gets plan_to_site instead. Another side's
;    unit gets FFFFh in the words 2 and 6 of its plan.
; 1: every unit of the other side (not the second half of a unit of two
;    parts) gets its worth for the side added to word 6 of its plan: byte
;    0 of the kind's kind_worth, 32h with C0h in the kind's word 6, 19h
;    for each of the kind's bytes 0Ah, 0Bh and 0Ch that is 0 (not with 20h
;    in its word 11h), the kind_worth of what is in its carrier (read from
;    the assessing side's row of the carrier, as the code has it), and
;    0Ah for each step its unit_exp is below 6. A kind with 1 in word 2 of
;    kind_worth that is nearer to the side's headquarters than its kind's
;    byte 0 (a unit with 4000h in unit_flags: that of the kind of its
;    carrier's unit) adds 12Ch, 2 to word 9 of computer_phase, and 12Ch to
;    the plans of the other side's units around it. (The neighbours are
;    taken of the halved map offset there, as the code has it; presumably
;    a slip of the original.)
; 2: with a unit of the side whose kind has 1 in word 2 of kind_worth, the
;    side's list of aims gets the other side's headquarters (worth
;    ten times byte 18h of its sites_40 record) and every record of
;    sites_400 and sites_100 that is in use and not the side's (worth 6Eh
;    times its byte 18h, 14h for each unit in the side's row, and for
;    sites_400 14h for every ten of its byte 16h or 17h), each of kind 1.
; 3: with such a unit on the other side, as many fields around the side's
;    own headquarters as word 9 of computer_phase says (at most 6; 1 with
;    less than ten units in byte 2 of the side's record), in the order of
;    guard_order, worth 78h plus 1Eh for each still to come, kind 3.
; 4: with a unit of the side whose kind has 280h in word 2 of kind_worth,
;    every unit with 4 in its word 6 and 2 in unit_flags, worth C8h, kind
;    4 (word 2 of the entry is the unit's number there, not a field).
; What the kinds 1, 3 and 4 of an aim lead to is computer_plan's (not read
; yet); "to take", "to guard" and "to fetch" are guesses from what is
; listed. The states were compared with the original (port/README.md).
; The list of a side's aims: the far pointer at byte 9 of its record of
; sides, entries of 6 bytes (word 0 the worth, word 2 a field's map offset
; or a unit, bytes 4 and 5 the kind, both the same as computer_assess
; writes them), their number in byte 6 of computer_phase. No bound is
; tested. The same buffer holds sites_list's words while state 0 runs.
; unit_worth(unit, far pointer to three words): each word is a byte of the
; unit's kind (0Bh, 0Ch, 0Ah in this order) times half the unit's count
; plus 1 (byte 2 of the unit, byte 3 with 4 in the kind's word 0Fh) times
; unit_exp plus 1 times an eighth of the kind's byte 2, the product
; divided by 20h. Read; translated and compared within computer_assess.
name S1FD8:00E8 unit_worth
; Where computer_assess has unit_worth put its three words.
name S331F:17F5 unit_worth_out
; unit_of_kind(mask, side): the first unit of the side (same_side with its
; unit_flags, 8000h clear) whose kind has a bit of the mask in word 2 of
; kind_worth; FFh for none. Read.
name S1FD8:02B2 unit_of_kind
; unit_reaches(field, unit, side, mode): 1 when path_find gives a way for
; the unit from its place to the field, else 0. Before that every field
; whose ground the kind can enter (byte 2 of the ground's record and byte
; 5 of the kind share a bit) is marked for the side in field_bits (1, the
; second side 2), but not a field with another side's unit when mode has
; 1, nor with an own unit other than the unit itself when mode has 2;
; the marks are cleared again. Read; compared within computer_assess.
name S1FD8:0368 unit_reaches
; sites_list(table, side, count): while the side has more than 0Eh in
; side_points, word 0Eh (the field) of every record of the table that is
; the side's and has not 8002h in word 19h is added as a word to the
; buffer behind the far pointer at byte 9 of the side's record of sides,
; counted in path_len. 0Fh is what a repair costs, so presumably the
; places a unit can be repaired at. Read.
name S202F:0BA7 sites_list
; plan_to_site(side, unit): the unit's plan becomes kind 0Ah with the
; worth 190h and as its field that of the nearest record of sites_400 of
; the side that unit_reaches (mode 1) finds a way to, the side's
; headquarters without one. The distance is taken of the map offsets not
; halved, as the code has it. Read; no call of it was compared.
name S202F:0EAA plan_to_site
; The units' plans: a record of 9 bytes for each unit, word 0 a field (or
; what the kind of plan needs), word 2 FFFFh until computer_queue has made
; the plan's steps and 1 after, word 4 the plan's worth (computer_queue
; takes the highest first), word 6 for another side's unit what it is
; worth as a target (computer_assess), byte 8 the kind of plan, 0 for
; none. A side uses unit_plans2 with 2 in its attack_pick, else
; unit_plans; some places write unit_plans2 whatever the side's table is.
name S39B6:09AB unit_plans
name S39B6:0132 unit_plans2
; A record of 6 bytes for each kind of unit: byte 0 (signed) what a unit
; of the kind is worth as a target, word 2 bits the computer chooses kinds
; by (1, 280h and 400h are tested; what they stand for is not known:
; presumably 1 a kind that can take a site, 400h one the computer builds).
; Bytes 1, 4 and 5 not read.
name S39B6:0000 kind_worth
; Six bytes: the order in which the fields around the headquarters are
; listed by computer_assess's state 3, as indices into neighbours.
name S3AE7:000E guard_order
; ---- computer_queue, read in full (2026-10-07, Mac): it makes the units'
; plans into steps, by byte 3 of the side's computer_phase, and returns 1
; when it has added steps that are to be carried out before it goes on
; (computer_turn then runs the list and calls it again in the same state).
; 0: word 2 of the plans of the side's units FFFFh (open), byte 7 and
;    word 9 of computer_phase 0.
; 1: the units in the side's sites get plans: with 1 in the side's
;    attack_pick plan_units_out, else plan_repairs (sites_100, sites_400,
;    sites_40).
; 2: the next unit of the side with a plan, from word 9 of computer_phase
;    on; none: on to 4.
; 3: that unit's plan when it is 3 (a step of kind 1 to the plan's field),
;    4 (nothing; the plan is given up), 0Ch (plan_move) or 0Eh (a step of
;    kind 2 against the unit on the plan's field); back to 2, with the
;    next unit when the plan is another.
; 4: the open plan with the highest word 4 among the side's units without
;    8200h in unit_flags; none: on to 6.
; 5: that plan: 1 and 0Dh plan_move; 2 a step of kind 2; 5 a step of kind
;    4 (the unit leaves its site); 6 a step of kind 6 (the call of
;    step_add at S1CC6:0567: a repair, see step_site_menu); 7
;    plan_approach; 9, 0Ah and 0Bh plan_move with the plan kept (only word
;    2 becomes 1); any other kind (3, 4, 8, 0Ch: the default at
;    S1CC6:07B7) is given up. Back to 4.
; 6 (S1CC6:07FC): building, not with 1 in attack_pick: for every free
;    place of the side's records of sites_400, while the side has more
;    than 3Dh in side_points and fewer than ten kinds were chosen,
;    build_list with the points above 3Dh and a kind drawn from
;    build_kinds by rand_range (up to a hundred tries) that has 400h in
;    word 2 of kind_worth: a step of kind 7, the kind's price (byte 3Fh)
;    taken off the count the state keeps. (The list of steps holds ten,
;    so later ones are dropped by step_add.)
; 7: a step of kind 3 (the round's end).
; 8: the phase becomes 20h (computer_assess) again, byte 3 0.
; The kinds of plan as computer_queue serves them: 1 and 0Dh to a field, as
; far as this round goes; 2 and 0Eh attack the unit on a field; 3 a move
; of one round to a field; 4 stay; 5 leave the site; 6 be repaired; 7 go
; next to a unit and attack what is there; 9, 0Ah, 0Bh to a field over
; several rounds; 0Ch a move served before the others (who writes which is
; computer_plan's). Translated; compared for the states and plans
; port/README.md names.
; plan_units_out(table, side, count): every unit in the side's row of the
; side's records of the table, without 24h in its word 6, gets the plan 5
; with the worth 7, in unit_plans. Read.
name S202F:04D9 plan_units_out
; plan_repairs(table, side, count): the same for the units whose
; unit_count is below byte 3 of their kind, while the side has more than
; 0Eh in side_points: the plan 6 with the worth 7, in unit_plans2. Read.
name S202F:05CB plan_repairs
; plan_move(unit, side): a part a call by byte 7 of computer_phase,
; returns 1 when it is through. 0 waits while 80h is set in game_state's
; word 4; 1, 2, 3 unit_reaches to the plan's field with the modes 3, 2 and
; 0 (the first with a way goes on to 4); 4 copies the way to the side's
; buffer of aims and its length to way_len; 5 move_range; 6
; move_targets_list; 7 a step of kind 1 to the first field of the way,
; from its end, that the unit can go to this round (other than the plan's
; field itself not a ground with 540h in its word 0 nor a field with a
; unit that has 1000h in unit_flags); no step without one. The second
; half of a unit of two parts stands for the first. Read.
name S202F:071E plan_move
; plan_approach(unit, side): the plan 7, whose word 0 is a unit: 0 waits
; as plan_move; 1 move_range; 2 the first free field around that unit, in
; the order of approach_order from the byte at 0Fh of the unit's record
; (the second side's at 10h; presumably the way it faces), that the unit
; can go to: a step of kind 1 there, the plan done, and for a unit of
; another side around that field that the kind can attack the plan 2
; against it in unit_plans2; without such a field the plan becomes 1 to
; the unit's field. Returns 1 from that state. Read; not compared (no
; call was dumped).
name S202F:000A plan_approach
; Six bytes added to a direction by plan_approach.
name S3AEA:000C approach_order
; The length of the way plan_move keeps between its states 4 and 7.
name S3AEA:0012 way_len
; Seven bytes: the step computer_queue and its helpers fill and hand to
; step_add. Only the bytes a kind needs are written, the others stay.
name S39B6:1264 step_draft
; rand_next(): the next number of the four words at rand_words (the word
; 0 as it was is returned; word 0 becomes itself xor word 2, shifted
; right with the top bit of word 6 coming in and its low bit going there;
; word 2 the old word 0). rand_range(lo, hi): its absolute value modulo
; the size of the range, plus lo. Read; compared within computer_queue's
; state 6. clock_seed sets rand_words.
name S2C9A:0008 rand_next
name DATA:0AF1 rand_words
name S0CB6:0713 rand_range
; ---- computer_plan, read in full (2026-10-07, Mac): it gives the side's
; units their plans, a part a call, by byte 4 of computer_phase (the
; state) and byte 7 (the step inside a state); returns 1 from state 0Ch.
; 0: with 2 in the side's attack_pick straight to 0Ch (nothing is planned
;    in that half; its table was filled in the other). Else plan_aim_kind 1.
; 1: the aim worth most among those of the kind plan_aim_kind (byte 5 of
;    the entry) becomes plan_aim and its kind chooses the state (1: 3, 2:
;    4, 3: 5, 4: 6; another: 2, which only strikes it out); without one
;    the next kind; after kind 5, or with no aims, on to 7. A state that
;    has served an aim sets byte 5 of its entry to 0 and comes back here.
; 3, an aim of kind 1 (a site to take): for every unit of the side whose
;    kind has 1 in word 2 of kind_worth, without C040h in unit_flags and
;    with a plan worth less than the aim, the length of its way there
;    (unit_reaches; 3E8h without one) into word 2 of its plan; the one
;    with the shortest way whose plan is also worth less than the aim's
;    worth less that length gets the plan 1 to the aim's field, worth
;    that difference. A kind with 20h in word 2 of kind_worth adds an aim
;    of kind 2 for the unit, worth ten less.
; 4, an aim of kind 2 (a unit to go with): as many units as byte 4 of
;    that unit's kind_worth says, each the one nearest to it by its way
;    among the side's units whose kind_worth word 2 shares one of the bits
;    1Ch with that unit's unit_flags, get the plan 7 (plan_approach) for
;    it, worth the aim's worth, which goes down by a third each time.
; 5, an aim of kind 3 (a field to hold): a unit of the side that stands on
;    it, with 40h in word 2 of its kind_worth and a plan worth less, gets
;    the plan 4 (stay); else the unit with 40h there that has the shortest
;    way gets the plan 1 to the field.
; 6, an aim of kind 4 (a unit, word 2 of the entry): plan_ride for it with
;    the kind 0Ah.
; 7, repairs: every unit of the side without C048h in unit_flags whose
;    unit_count is below byte 3 of its kind: the last field sites_list
;    gives (only that one is tried), worth 0Fh, or 46h plus ten times
;    unit_exp for a unit with a count below 5 and unit_exp above 1; with
;    a way of at most the kind's byte 0 fields (unit_reaches, mode 1) the
;    worth is doubled and the unit gets the plan 1 there when that beats
;    its plan; further off, or without a way, plan_ride with the kind 9
;    (not for a kind with 380h in word 2 of kind_worth).
; 8: word 2 of the plan of every unit of the other side becomes what can
;    attack it: 1 with C0h in its kind's word 6, 2, 4 and 8 for a 0 in
;    the kind's bytes 0Ah, 0Ch and 0Bh.
; 9, the units that fire from afar (2 in word 2 of kind_worth, not C200h
;    in unit_flags): attack_range with the kind's bytes 9 and 8 (above 1)
;    marks what they reach (4, the second side 8, in field_bits); with a
;    field marked the unit gets the plan 4 (stay), worth 64h, and in
;    unit_plans2 the plan 0Eh against the marked field whose unit has the
;    highest word 6 (the byte on a field without a unit indexes the plans
;    all the same, as the code has it).
; 0Ah, the attacks: again and again the unit of the other side with the
;    highest word 6 whose word 2 is not negative (plan_target). Every unit
;    of the side that is not unit_outmatched, has a plan worth less than
;    that, stands nearer than half its kind's byte 0, can attack it (the
;    kind's word 6 and the target's unit_flags share one of 3Ch) and has
;    not 40h in the kind's word 6 is listed, after move_range, for each of
;    the six fields around the target it stands on or could go to (free,
;    not field_pinched, not a ground with 540h, not the aim of any plan):
;    six lists of up to 14h units in the buffer of aims, their lengths at
;    78h there. Then up to four of the fields are given a unit (state
;    words, fields and units at 0, 14h and 28h of the side's work buffer;
;    plan_count counts): first units whose unit_flags fit the target's
;    word 2, then one opposite a field taken, a pair on opposite fields,
;    one between two taken, any. A unit chosen gets the plan 3 to its
;    field (4 when it stands there), worth the target's word 6, and in
;    unit_plans2 the plan 2 against the target's field. The target's word
;    2 becomes FFFFh and the next is looked for.
; 0Bh, the units still without a plan (not C000h in unit_flags, not 20h
;    in word 6, not 380h in kind_worth): word 2 of every other unit's plan
;    becomes its distance (for the side's own units that of their plan's
;    field); the unit of the other side with the highest word 6 that the
;    kind can attack and that has a way to it gives the plan 1 to its
;    field, worth 0Ah; else the nearest unit of the side with a plan worth
;    more than 0Ah (not the plans 6, 8, 0Ch) gives the plan 1 to that
;    plan's field; else plan_ride with the kind 0Bh, worth 46h, to the
;    side's headquarters.
; 0Ch: bytes 4 and 6 of computer_phase 0 (the aims are used up).
; The aims' kinds, then: 1 a site to take, 2 a unit to go with, 3 a field
; to hold, 4 a unit to fetch. Translated; compared for the states and
; steps port/README.md names.
; The variables computer_plan keeps between calls: the target of state
; 0Ah, the unit at hand, the kind of aim at hand, the aim at hand, how
; many of sites_list's fields are left, the worth and the field state 7
; hands to plan_ride, the count of fields of state 0Ah, and the other
; unit of state 0Bh.
name S3AEB:0004 plan_target
name S3AEB:0005 plan_unit
name S3AEB:0006 plan_aim_kind
name S3AEB:0008 plan_aim
name S3AEB:000A plan_sites_left
name S3AEB:000C plan_worth
name S3AEB:000E plan_field
name S3AEB:0010 plan_count
name S3AEB:0012 plan_other
; plan_ride(side, unit, worth, kind, field): a carrier for the unit, a
; part a call by byte 8 of computer_phase, returns 1 when through. 0: a
; unit with 4 in its word 6 goes on at 5; 1 move_range and 2
; move_targets_list for the unit; 3 a field among those with a unit whose
; plan is `kind` already: the unit gets the plan 0Ch there and that unit's
; plan is worth `worth` more; 4 one with a unit without a plan: the same,
; and that unit gets the plan `kind` to `field`; 5 the next carrier of the
; side from ride_carrier on (1000h in unit_flags, 380h in word 2 of its
; kind_worth, a plan worth less and not 9, 0Ah, 0Bh or 0Dh, its record of
; carriers sharing one of the bits FC0h in word 19h with the unit's word
; 6); 6 with a way to the unit it gets the plan 0Dh to the unit's field,
; else the next carrier is tried. The kinds: 9 to a site for repair, 0Ah
; to fetch the aim's unit, 0Bh home. Read.
name S2407:0007 plan_ride
name S3AEC:0004 ride_carrier
; unit_outmatched(unit, other): FFFFh when the unit's count (byte 2, byte
; 3 with 4 in its kind's word 0Fh) is more than two below the other's and
; its unit_exp below 3, else 0. Read.
name S1FD8:0002 unit_outmatched
; field_pinched(field, side): 1 for a field with more than three units of
; the other side around it or with two of them on opposite sides;
; neighbours is kept. Read.
name S202F:0C79 field_pinched
; unit_chosen(unit, side): 1 when the unit is among the six bytes at 28h
; of the side's work buffer (the units computer_plan's state 0Ah has
; chosen for the fields around its target). Read.
name S202F:0E3C unit_chosen
; computer_step(side): carries on the step byte 46h of computer_steps
; names, by its kind through the table at S1E4B:0381, with the map offset
; of the side's cursor (word 0 of its view): 1 step_move (bytes 1 and 3, a
; unit and a field), 2 step_attack (bytes 1 and 3, two units), 3
; step_end_round (word 0Eh of the side's record of sites_40), 4
; step_unit_out (byte 1, a unit), 5 cursor_script (word 1, a field), 6
; step_site_menu (byte 1, a unit), 7 step_build (bytes 1 and 3, a kind
; and a record of sites_400). A handler returns not 0 when its step is
; done and byte 46h goes up. Returns 0, or FFFFh at the list's end (the
; list is emptied). In runs the kinds 1, 2, 3, 4 and 7 came up, 5 and 6
; never. Read; translated, and compared for those five kinds
; (port/README.md).
name S1E4B:012E computer_step
; computer_input(side): puts the next word of input into computer_out (0
; when there is none) from the code at the script's place: a code below
; 80h is one word, script_bits by the code; 80h and above is a sequence of
; script_gestures, a word a call. Returns 1 when the script is at its end
; after that (and empties it), else 0. Read; the port's translation agreed
; with the original on the calls dumped (port/README.md).
name S1E4B:0001 computer_input
; step_add(side, step): copies the 7 bytes of a step to the end of the
; side's list in computer_steps and ends the list behind it; nothing with
; ten steps there. Read.
name S1E4B:038F step_add
; The step handlers and their helpers, named above with side_income
; ("The step handlers behind the table at S1E4B:0381"), as read on the Mac
; (2026-10-07), one paragraph each:
; step_move(side, cursor, unit, aim, the side's computer_steps), a step of
; kind 1: by byte 47h, 0 waits while 80h is set in game_state's word 4; 1
; cursor_script to the unit's place; 2 the code 80h (button and up: the
; gesture of a move); 3 cursor_step towards the aim until the cursor is
; there; 4 move_target for the cursor's field, and 8 set in word 0 of the
; side's record of sides when the field is not marked for the side in
; field_bits (1, the second side 2) or move_target refuses it, then the
; code 5 (the button); 5 nothing; 6 the code 5 again; 7 done. Read; the
; port's translation agreed with the original (port/README.md).
; step_attack(side, cursor, unit, target, steps), kind 2: 0 cursor_script
; to the unit; 1 the code 80h; 2 cursor_step towards the target unit's
; place; 3 the button, and on to 5 when the target's field is marked for
; the side's attack in field_bits (4, the second side 8), else 8 in the
; side's word 0; 4 the button; 5 done. Read and translated; no call of it
; was seen in a run.
; step_end_round(side, cursor, field, steps), kind 3, with word 0Eh of the
; side's record of sites_40 (its headquarters): 0 cursor_script to the
; field; 1 cursor_step towards the field a row below it; 2 the code 82h
; (button and left) once 80h is clear in game_state's word 4; 3 waits for
; 4 in the side's computer_phase, which game_loop sets after the round's
; end, and clears it; 4 done. So the computer ends its round below its
; headquarters and waits there. Read; translated and compared.
; step_unit_out(side, cursor, unit, steps), kind 4: a unit leaves the site
; or carrier it is in. 0 unit_holder into holder_ptr (none: done); 1
; cursor_script to the holder's field (word 0Eh); 2 the code 82h; 3 the
; codes 2 or 1 (down, up) until word 0Eh of the view is the unit's place in
; the side's row; 4 waits while 80h is set in game_state's word 4; 5 the
; code 80h; 6 nothing; 7 move_targets_list with the far pointer at byte 9
; of the side's record of sides: step_target_field becomes its first
; field, or with path_len 0 the holder's own field and 8 in the side's
; word 0; 8 cursor_step towards it; 9 and 0Ah the button; 0Bh the code
; 83h, and done at once (the code runs on into the state 0Ch, which only
; a step left in that state would reach). The unit's place is the last of
; the row's seven that holds it, 0 without. Read; translated and compared
; (port/README.md).
; step_site_menu(side, cursor, unit, steps), kind 6: as step_unit_out up
; to the unit's row in its holder (the pointer at S3AE8:0023), then the
; code 81h (button and down) and the code 83h, done with that call. Button
; and down in a site's list is the repair (game_loop's state 2), and
; computer_queue adds this step for the plan 6, which plan_repairs gives a
; unit below its full count in a site: so this is the computer's repair.
; No step of this kind came up in 1500 s on 16 maps. Read and
; translated, not compared.
; step_build(side, cursor, kind, site, steps), kind 7: cursor_script to
; the field of the record `site` of sites_400 (pointer at S3AE8:0027), the
; code 82h, the list's row to the last free place (FFh) of the side's row
; of seven (the codes 2 or 1), 82h again, the code 2 (down) while the
; kind's place in build_kinds (the last among build_count, 0 without) is
; above the view's word 0Eh plus word 20h, 82h, 83h, done with the next
; call. Read; translated and compared.
; unit_holder(side, unit): a far pointer to the record that has the unit
; in the side's row, looked for with rec_find_unit in sites_400 (10
; records), sites_100 (10), carriers (70) and sites_40 (2); FFFFh:FFFFh
; for none. Read.
; rec_find_unit(side, unit, table, count): the number of the first of the
; table's 1Ch-byte records, without 2 and 8000h in word 19h, that has the
; unit among the seven places of the side's row; FFFFh for none. Read.
; move_targets_list(buffer, side, unit), as read on the Mac: path_len 0,
; the unit into move_rec, then column by column every field marked for the
; side in field_bits (1, the second side 2) for which move_target gives 0
; is written as a map offset to the buffer and counted in path_len, up to
; 316h. Translated and compared with step_unit_out's state 7.
; cursor_scroll(side, column, row): one move of the side's view (its
; words 0Ch and 0Eh) towards the place that has the field five columns
; and four rows in, kept inside the map and even: the codes 3 or 4 (left,
; right) and 1 or 2 into computer_script. Returns 1 when the view is
; there or the field is off the map. Read; translated and compared.
; cursor_step(side, cursor, field): the same for the cursor, a field a
; call towards the field. Returns 1 when it is there, or the field is off
; the map or in its last column or row. Read; translated and compared.
; cursor_script(side, cursor, field, the side's computer_steps): takes the
; cursor to the field, a part a call, by byte 48h of the steps: 0 chooses
; (4 at once when the field is less than five columns and rows away or
; byte 18h of the view is set); 1 the code 83h (button and right); 2
; cursor_scroll until the view is there; 3 the button; 4 cursor_step until
; the cursor is there; 5 done, returns 1. Read; translated and compared.
name S1E4B:128E cursor_script
; The input word of each code 0 to 9: nothing, up, down, left, right, the
; button, and the four diagonals.
name S3AE8:0004 script_bits
; The sequences of the codes 80h to 84h, three bytes each, ended by FFh:
; the button with up, down, left or right and then nothing, and the button
; twice.
name S3AE8:000E script_gestures

; The interrupts' segment S27FE (read 2026-10-08 on the Mac; input_tick,
; input_side0/1 and key_irq are translated in port/src/input.c and
; compared through port/tests/play_test.sh, the rest is read only;
; docs/HANDOFF.md, "The port's program plays a battle by itself" and
; "The port's own clock").
; input_install: pit_install, then input_tick is given to the timer with
; the period 3FFFh (pit_add), S2B9B:000A is called (not read), and
; interrupt 24h is set to crit_error, the old one kept at S27FE:000E.
name S27FE:0013 input_install
; input_remove: interrupt 24h back, then pit_remove.
name S27FE:0060 input_remove
; input_tick: the routine the timer calls 72.8 times a second. Counts the
; word at DATA:0308 game_loop waits by; a key the BIOS has (INT 16h) or the
; one key_irq left at DATA:0B2B goes into the record at DATA:045C; on
; every fourth call (DATA:0B19) the joysticks and the mouse are read and
; the two sides' input records filled (input_side0, input_side1).
name S27FE:008C input_tick
; input_side0, input_side1 (SI the five bytes found now, DI those of the
; call before, BX the counts of holds and gaps, BP the side's record):
; with the side's joystick switched on the directions and the button come
; from it, else from the side's table of keys (input_keys).
name S27FE:0175 input_side0
name S27FE:020E input_side1
; input_keys (AX the table of keys, seven bytes a key): the bytes of every
; key of the table that is held are ORed into the five at SI, the mouse is
; asked for the record the word at DATA:0418 names (input_mouse), and
; input_record follows.
name S27FE:029E input_keys
; input_record: what was found goes into the record at BP: FFh into byte 8
; when the button is up, the directions into bytes 0 to 3, FFh into byte 4
; for the button and into byte 5 for a second press within 19h calls
; (bytes 6 and 7 keep how far that has come); then the five pairs of
; counts at BX.
name S27FE:0320 input_record
; input_mouse: the mouse's part of a record: its distance from the middle
; (A0h, 64h) beyond the word at DATA:0420 gives a direction, the word at
; DATA:0444 the button. Read, not translated, not seen in a run.
name S27FE:03D4 input_mouse
; mouse_center: puts the mouse back to the middle (INT 33h, 4) unless a
; button is held.
name S27FE:04D0 mouse_center
; key_irq: interrupt 9. The byte read goes to DATA:0B2B, the key's bit in
; the 16 bytes at DATA:0B1B is cleared for a key down and set for one up;
; nothing is passed on to the BIOS.
name S27FE:04F4 key_irq
; crit_error: interrupt 24h while the game runs: 2 into the word at
; DATA:0B17 and AL 0. Found as the vector input_install sets, not seen in
; a run.
code S27FE:055C crit_error
; key_install, key_remove: interrupt 9 to key_irq and back (the old one at
; S27FE:000A, the byte at S27FE:0012 says it is set).
name S27FE:056C key_install
name S27FE:05AB key_remove
; pit_install: the timer's interrupt 8 goes to pit_irq, which shares the
; timer's counts out among up to sixteen routines, each with a period of
; counts (32 bits: the words at DATA:0D1F and 0D3F), what is left of it
; (0D5F, 0D7F), a far pointer (0DFF) and a flag that it is due (0D9F);
; DATA:0D1D is the last one's index, 0E47 the shortest period, which the
; timer is set to. The first routine is pit_bios with the period 10000h.
name S27FE:0606 pit_install
; pit_bios: calls the interrupt 8 that was there (DATA:0E43), which counts
; the BIOS's ticks.
name S27FE:0692 pit_bios
; pit_remove: interrupt 8 back and the timer to its full period.
name S27FE:0699 pit_remove
; pit_irq: takes the period the timer ran with off what each routine has
; left; a routine with nothing left is due, gets its period added and is
; called, the last added first. Then the timer is set to the shortest
; period when that has changed. So the BIOS's count of ticks, from which
; clock_seed starts the random numbers, depends on which routines there
; are: besides input_tick the two of S30EF (presumably the sound's). From
; the number of input_tick's calls alone the count is found only to within
; a tick (tried on the logs of three runs: the fraction between the two
; is another in each run).
name S27FE:06D2 pit_irq
; pit_add (DX:AX the routine, CX:BX its period): returns its number in AX.
; pit_del (AX the number). pit_period (AX the number, CX:BX the new
; period). Read; pit_del and pit_period's callers were not looked at.
name S27FE:0783 pit_add
name S27FE:07E8 pit_del
name S27FE:0882 pit_period

; screen_open(w, h, n, dword size, pages): called once by game_loop at
; its start (S066A:014D, with 320, 200, 4, 2518h, 1). Keeps INT 10h
; AH=0Fh's AX (the BIOS's mode and columns) at DATA:0346, clears A000:0
; (7FFFh words, all planes), takes the CRTC's port from 40:63 (DATA:0AF9,
; 0AFB one more, 0AFD six more), sets the mode (S298E:007C), keeps size at
; DATA:0342 and pages at DATA:034E, calls pages_set, then screen_clear,
; page_flip, screen_clear with colour 0 (DATA:00DA). S298E:007C decides
; by the height only (it compares the width with AX after loading AX with
; DATA's segment): 200 lines are mode 13h with the DAC made black, chain-4
; and the CRTC's word mode and double words off (Mode X), 320 by 200,
; screen_pitch 50h, DATA:02F2 (bytes a page) 3E80h, DATA:02F6 FA00h, and
; the offsets of F0h lines at DATA:00F8; other heights set a mode of 360
; by 240 or 480 from the CRTC tables at S298E:02B4 and 02CC (not met). n
; is not used. Read whole; translated (port/src/screen.c) and compared on
; its call on map 0 (port/README.md).
name S298E:000D screen_open
; pages_set: the pages' segments for the height at DATA:02E6: with two
; pages (DATA:034E) A400h is drawn (screen_seg) and A000h shown
; (DATA:0356); further segments and counts at DATA:0322 to 0330 and
; 035C to 0368 (A7E8h, 4, AC58h, AC4Eh; what they are was not looked at).
; Read whole; translated, compared through screen_open.
name S2A10:0006 pages_set
; screen_clear: DATA:02F2 bytes of all four planes of the page drawn made
; the colour DATA:00DA. Read; translated, compared through screen_open.
name S28D9:000C screen_clear
; page_flip: the page drawn and the one shown change places; the CRTC's
; start address is set to the new shown one between two retraces. Without
; DATA:00F6 the words at DATA:0322 to 0328 change places with 032A to 0330
; first. With DATA:0463 and 0465 both FFFFh it calls S2B51:002A first,
; which builds the header of a PBM picture of 320 by 200 in a block of
; 190h bytes (presumably to save the screen to a file; not read further,
; not met). Read; translated, compared through screen_open.
name S2974:0002 page_flip
; page_copy: the page shown (screen_shown) copied to the page drawn
; (screen_seg), page_size bytes in each plane through the latches (write
; mode 1, map mask all four planes), write mode 0 after it. Called by
; game_loop after page_flip at a battle's beginning, so both pages hold
; the drawn views. Read; translated (port/src/screen.c), compared at its
; call on map 0 and map 8 (port/README.md).
name S28DC:000A page_copy
name DATA:0356 screen_shown
name DATA:0346 bios_mode_old
name DATA:0AF9 crtc_port
name DATA:02F2 page_size
name DATA:00F8 line_offsets
; retrace_wait: waits until the screen's next vertical retrace begins
; (8 in the byte read from the port the word at DATA:0AFD names); display_wait until one is over.
; The waits and the changes of the screen's colours count their steps by
; these: 70 a second in the runs.
name S2945:000A retrace_wait
name S2947:0006 display_wait
; wait_frames(n): n + 1 calls of retrace_wait.
name S0CB6:0001 wait_frames
; wait_input(n): the routine that waits for the player. While the first
; side's button (byte 4 of the record behind DATA:00A6) is held or the
; key's word 4 (behind DATA:00BE) is 1 it clears both and waits three
; frames (wait_frames(3)); then it clears both and waits again in steps
; of three, n counted down by 3 until it is below 0, as long as neither
; comes. Returns 1 for the key of entry 0 of the table of keys or when the
; time ran out, else 0. Seen with 96h after a fight's marks on the
; map and before its pictures (S131D:1CAE, after six wait_frames(6) and a
; wait_frames(0Ch); in m8_site ended after 42 steps by a key of the
; script), and with 50h in attacks_run for a fight without pictures (not
; seen in a run).
name S0CB6:0036 wait_input
; start_setup(far pointer): called once at the program's start (from
; S066A:0294 on; when, against the menu, was not looked at). Sets the screen's record behind DATA:0092 to
; 320 by 200, makes two file names (file_name with 0Ah and with 5) and
; loads and shows them (L2BAA, S28A5:000C: not read), then sets the far
; pointer to the table of keys S331F:0292 at S331F:02D3 and copies twelve
; of its entries to S331F:02C7. The port does the last part
; (start_setup in port/src/battle.c).
name S1650:0003 start_setup
; fade_grey(far palette): makes of the 300h bytes of colours a grey of
; each ((2 * first + second + third) / 4, into the buffer behind
; S3303:0028) and changes the screen's colours to it in 20h and then 40h
; steps, a retrace_wait each. game_loop calls it before attacks_run when
; the side that ends the round has 0 in byte 15h of its record in sides.
; fade_back(far palette): the way back after attacks_run, 40h and 20h
; steps. Together 192 retraces, 2.74 s: what a round's end without fights
; lasts in the runs (pass 291 of m8_site: 96 calls of retrace_wait before
; attacks_run and 96 after it). The other branch (site_taken 1, see
; there) calls fade_out and fade_in when fight pictures are on.
name S0E56:21D8 fade_grey
name S0E56:1F91 fade_back
; pal_level(level, far palette): sets the screen's 256 colours to the
; palette's (300h bytes of 0 to 255) times level / 100h, a quarter of it
; to the port 3C9h. After each colour's first two bytes it waits, with
; interrupts off, for the next beginning of a horizontal blank (bit 0 of
; the port 3DAh clear, then set): a call lasts 256 scan lines, 8.1 ms in
; the runner (449 lines a retrace; its bit pulses in the vertical blank
; too, on a real screen presumably longer: not checked), and the timer's
; interrupt is held back for that long.
name S2AFE:000C pal_level
; fade_in: pal_level with the levels 0, 4, ... FCh and the palette at
; DATA:04E3 (64 calls, 0.52 s in the runs); fade_out: the levels FFh,
; FBh, ... 3. Both read and write nothing else. Besides the round's end
; they are called by the fight's panel, the pictures of events (S1A39)
; and the menus (S1650, S167A). Both and pal_level translated
; (port/src/screen.c); fade_in compared through battle_begin's end.
name S28E0:0004 fade_in
name S28E0:002B fade_out
; inputs_release(1, wait): clears the key's word 4 (behind DATA:00BE),
; byte 4 of both sides' input records (DATA:00A6, 00B6) and the words 30h
; and 34h behind DATA:00C2 (presumably the mouse's buttons) and waits
; wait_frames(5), again as long as one of them was set since: at least
; twice. With `wait` not 0 it then waits until one is set (that part was
; not read to its end). Called with 0 at the beginning of event_picture.
name S167A:2F83 inputs_release
; event_picture(far, far, kind, ...): the picture shown for an event.
; After inputs_release it goes by kind: C8h to D0h through the table at
; S1A39:02B3, others to S1A39:059D twice (not read). CAh and CBh, the
; site taken by the first or the second side (attacks_run's order 4),
; both go to site_picture, with 0 or A0h as its first argument.
name S1A39:0001 event_picture
; site_picture: loads its files (S1A39:034C with 3 and the names at
; S3812:086C; not read), starts a sound (S2F39:0F87, not read), then
; shows the frames of the stream at S3812:0888 until S2982:0002 returns
; FFFF:FFFF for the next one; a frame lasts until the timer's count
; (DATA:0308, set to 0 before it) is 6, tested after each retrace_wait.
; Then wait_frames(C8h) and S2F39:1058(14h) (not read). How many frames
; the stream has was not read: the frames lasted 1.84 s in the one run
; with a site taken (m0_hq), some 22 of them. It reads no input.
name S1A39:1906 site_picture
; fight_pictures: the fight shown as pictures (called by fight_show with
; the counts before and after). Keeps its arguments in S3AEE, calls
; clock_seed(0), loads its file (S2532:0357) and sets up (0.53 s in the
; runs), clears the key's word 4 (S2532:0131) and runs fight_frames;
; then pal_level from the level reached down to 0 in steps of 4 and
; S2F39:09C9 for eight channels (presumably the sound's; not read).
; Its parts (2026-10-08, by their calls only; lines of the listing):
; S2532:01C2 (54) and 0258 (58, once per side with its kind) set up
; S3AEE without calls; 02D6 (42) clears the screen; 0357 (362) loads the
; picture's files (file_load_size, lib_read, L2C39) and 0755 (112) more
; pictures (lib_read, L03B8); 0877 (475) draws the start (lbm_show,
; pic_draw, text_draw, the flags 1A8F/1BC3, S2532:1CF9, S29C1:001F,
; pal_level); 1FD6 (133) and 1E66 (156) load further files (L2B66,
; L2BAA); 1DD3 (58) is the error exit (input_remove, key_remove, L1851,
; L2585, S2B7F:000E, S2CC9:0002); 211E (64) the sound (S2F39). Not read
; are the blitters S2AF3:000A, S294A:000A, S29C1:001F, S292E:000A,
; S2B76:0004. Nothing of S2532 is translated.
name S2532:0008 fight_pictures
; fight_frames: the frames 1 to 2EDh (the count at S3AEE:0680). A frame
; below 40h first sets the colours (pal_level, level 4 * frame + 3: the
; picture comes up); then the figures' moves are worked out, and at the
; frame's end the key's word 4 is tested: not 0 ends the pictures at once
; (a key, not a side's button). The screen is drawn and shown
; (S2AF3:000A, not read) in every second frame at least. In the runs the
; 749 frames lasted 13.58 and 13.71 s (18 ms a frame; the drawing's time,
; not counted). The calls of rand_next come from S2532:17D1 (not read
; further, see HANDOFF).
name S2532:0CAA fight_frames
; fight_frames' parts: S2532:17D1 (174) shares the losses out among the
; volleys left and calls rand_next (see HANDOFF), 1970 (111) marks the
; figures that fall, 072A (22) is called from the frames and from 0755.
